      "name": "ProcessCompositeUnitGraphics",
      "signature": "void ProcessCompositeUnitGraphics(uint * pCompositeUnit)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Processes and renders composite unit graphics components.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input composite unit pointer for null\n2. Check unit visibility flags using gdwBitMasks_exref bitmasks\n3. Extract base width (field 5) and height (field 6) from composite unit\n4. Validate graphics info pointer at offset 0x2e exists\n5. Iterate through graphics info linked list to find matching frame\n6. Match by animation type (field 8) and direction lookup (field 9)\n7. Validate COF (Component Object File) data pointer exists\n8. Extract frame position from unit coordinates (field 1 & 2)\n9. Calculate frame data offset using COF header and position\n10. First pass: count valid components and calculate maximum width\n11. For each component in COF data validate component type < 16\n12. Initialize component structure with unit reference and coordinates\n13. Call thunk_FUN_10001960 to set up component rendering context\n14. Call Ordinal_10055 to prepare component for rendering\n15. Call Ordinal_10040 to get component width and update maximum\n16. Second pass: render all components if count > 0\n17. For each component call Ordinal_10079 to perform actual rendering\n\nParameters:\npCompositeUnit (uint*): Pointer to composite unit structure containing:\n  Field 0: Visibility flags\n  Field 1: X coordinate (byte)\n  Field 2: Y coordinate with direction in upper bits\n  Field 5: Base width\n  Field 6: Base height \n  Field 8: Animation type identifier\n  Field 9: Direction index for lookup table\n  Field 0x2e: Pointer to graphics info linked list\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, performs rendering side effects\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Null pointer validation with assertion and exit(-1)\n- Missing graphics info assertion and exit(-1)\n- Missing COF data assertion and exit(-1)\n- Component type >= 16 assertion and exit(-1)\n- Empty COF (no components) returns immediately\n- Zero valid components returns without rendering\n\nError Handling:\nAll error conditions trigger Ordinal_10021 assertion with source file and line\nfollowed by FUN_100149f1(0xffffffff) which exits the process\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x44e - Line number for null unit pointer check\n0x45e - Line number for null graphics info check  \n0x466 - Line number for null COF data check\n0x2ad - Line number for null frame data check\n0x429 - Line number for invalid component type check\n0x475 - Line number for component type check in render loop\n0x2e - Offset to graphics info pointer in composite unit\n0x14 - Offset to COF data in graphics info node\n0x1c - COF header size before component data",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:d71d3963a51332cd6946d27f82e6d4246150c678ed28981486d56173b0ac6bdd",
