      "name": "RenderAccountListGrid",
      "signature": "int RenderAccountListGrid(int * pListData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Renders account list entries in a 6-column grid layout.\n\nClassification: Callback/Handler - Render callback stored in list data structure at offset 0x1C.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate list data type is 0xc (D2WIN_ACCOUNTLIST), assert and abort if not\n2. Check visibility flags (bits 0 and 3) and list head pointer, return 0 if conditions not met\n3. Set active font from pListData[0x14] (font index)\n4. Initialize 512-character Unicode buffer for text conversion\n5. Cache layout parameters: nBaseX from pListData[0xC], nSubtypeY from pListData[0x10], nY from pListData[0x18]\n6. Get current font height from GetCurrentFontProperty()\n7. Iterate through linked list (next pointer at node offset 0x34):\n   a. Check if item index is within visible range [scrollOffset, scrollOffset + 24)\n   b. Calculate grid X position: nBaseX + (index % 6) * 0x78 (120 pixels per column)\n   c. Calculate grid Y position: fontHeight + (nSubtypeY - nY) + (index / 6) * 0x14 (20 pixels per row)\n   d. Set clip region for item icon area (28x14 pixels)\n   e. Convert account name (ANSI at node base) to Unicode\n   f. Render text at (X + 32, Y) with no line height adjustment\n   g. If current node matches selected node (pListData[0x44]), draw selection highlight rectangle\n   h. Increment item index and continue to next node\n8. Return 1 on successful render, 0 if visibility conditions not met\n\nParameters:\n- pListData (ECX): Pointer to account list data structure (type 0xc)\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Successfully rendered visible account list items\n- 0: Visibility flags not set or list is empty\n\nStructure Layout (AccountListData at pListData):\nOffset  Size  Field              Description\n0x00    4     dwType             Must be 0xc for account list\n0x08    4     dwFlags            Visibility/enabled bitmask\n0x0C    4     nBaseX             X coordinate for grid base\n0x10    4     nSubtypeY          Subtype Y offset\n0x18    4     nY                 Y coordinate base\n0x40    4     pListHead          Head of linked list (account nodes)\n0x44    4     pSelectedNode      Currently selected node\n0x48    4     nScrollOffset      First visible item index\n0x50    4     nFontIndex         Font to use for rendering\n\nAccount Node Layout (at szCurrentNode):\nOffset  Size  Field              Description\n0x00    52    szAccountName      ANSI account name string\n0x34    4     pNextNode          Pointer to next node in list\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xc: Account list type identifier\n- 0x78 (120): Grid column width in pixels (6 columns)\n- 0x14 (20): Grid row height in pixels\n- 0x18 (24): Maximum visible items in grid (6 columns x 4 rows)\n- 0x1c (28): Icon clip width\n- 0x0e (14): Icon clip height\n- 0x20 (32): Text X offset from column start\n- 0x55: Clip validation flag for icon area\n- 0xff: Clip validation flag for selection highlight\n\nDecompiler Artifacts:\n- extraout_var (undefined3): Spurious high bytes from CONCAT31 operation in font height calculation\n\nVariable Mappings (SSA temporaries):\n- nItemIndex: Loop counter for item position in list\n- nBaseX: X coordinate base loaded from pListData[0x0C]\n- szCurrentNode: Current linked list node being rendered\n- byFontHeight: Font height from GetCurrentFontProperty()\n- nSubtypeY: Y offset from pListData[0x10]\n- nY: Base Y from pListData[0x18]\n- nGridX/nGridY: Calculated grid cell coordinates\n- awUnicodeBuffer: 512-char Unicode buffer for text conversion\n\nCross-References:\n- Called from CreateUnit as render callback (stored at offset 0x1C)\n- Uses SelectListNodeByGridPosition for mouse selection logic",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04b",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:d80f095151998c391b43c83e3f39b98cd13271b79424c8077254a55badb91888",
