      "name": "ValidateAndClearGameStatePointers",
      "signature": "void ValidateAndClearGameStatePointers(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Validates and clears three critical game state pointers, reporting errors through validation handler.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load g_pGameStateManager into ECX\n2. Test if pointer is non-NULL\n3. If non-NULL, call ReportValidationError with pointer as parameter\n4. Clear g_pGameStateManager to NULL\n5. Load g_pPlayerInventory into ECX\n6. Test if pointer is non-NULL\n7. If non-NULL, call ReportValidationError with pointer as parameter\n8. Clear g_pPlayerInventory to NULL\n9. Load g_pWorldState into ECX\n10. Test if pointer is non-NULL\n11. If non-NULL, call ReportValidationError with pointer as parameter\n12. Clear g_pWorldState to NULL\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function executes regardless of pointer state; early return occurs only at validation points\n- All three pointers must be cleared even if one validation fails\n- ReportValidationError may have side effects not visible in decompiled code\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x6fbf6758: Address of g_pGameStateManager global pointer\n- 0x6fbf675c: Address of g_pPlayerInventory global pointer  \n- 0x6fbf6760: Address of g_pWorldState global pointer",
