      "name": "SearchGlyphDataBinary",
      "signature": "int * SearchGlyphDataBinary(ushort wCharCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int *",
      "comment": "Binary search for character glyph data in East Asian font tables.\n\nUsed as g_pfnValueProcessor callback for East Asian locales (Chinese, Japanese,\nKorean) and font ID 0xd. Unlike GetCharacterGlyphData which uses direct array\nindexing for ASCII fonts, this performs binary search through sorted Unicode\nglyph tables containing thousands of entries.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize search bounds: low=0, high=(glyph count - 1)\n2. Loop with iteration limit (max 1001 iterations for safety)\n3. Calculate mid index, compare character codes\n4. If match found, return pointer to glyph entry\n5. Adjust bounds: if target < mid, search lower half; else upper half\n6. If not found, return pointer to default glyph at offset 0x1b2 (entry 31)\n\nParameters:\n- wCharCode (ushort via CX): Unicode character code to look up\n\nReturns:\n- int *: Pointer to 14-byte glyph data entry in font table\n         Returns default glyph (offset 0x1b2) if not found\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x14 (20): Font cache entry stride (5 DWORDs per font slot)\n- 0xe (14): Glyph entry size in bytes\n- 0x3e9 (1001): Maximum search iterations (safety limit)\n- 0x1b2 (434): Offset to default/fallback glyph entry (31 * 14)\n- +8: Offset to glyph count field in font header\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n- g_nCurrentFontIndex: Currently active font slot index\n- g_pFontHandles: Font header pointers array (glyph count at +8)\n- g_pFontDataPtrs: Font glyph data pointers array\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GetCharacterGlyphData: Direct lookup for ASCII/Western fonts\n- SetActiveFont: Sets g_pfnValueProcessor to this or GetCharacterGlyphData",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:4b8e46295c11f3eac4b5877ce294ebab47a34c9040cdfa1ae2cefa9ede772138",
