      "comment": "Renders text with cel-shaded character animations, parsing embedded escape codes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate nMaxVal >= 0 (early exit if invalid max width)\n2. Call GetWindowMode() to determine rendering mode\n3. Get string length via Unicode::strlen (indirect call through g_pfnstrlen)\n4. Zero-initialize 72-byte CEL file cache (18 DWORDs via STOSD.REP)\n5. Iterate through Unicode string character by character\n6. On 0xFF escape byte: parse escape code type\n   6a. 'a' color code: skip 3 characters, advance position\n   6b. 'b' animation code: lookup CEL data, render via GfxInterfaceCall84\n7. On 0x0A (newline): calculate line height, advance Y, reset X\n8. For normal glyphs: lookup CEL data, validate bounds, render via GfxInterface_DrawConditional\n9. Advance X position by glyph width (offset +3 in glyph struct)\n\nParameters:\n- pszString (Unicode*): Unicode string with embedded 0xFF escape codes\n- dwX (uint): X starting position in pixels (ECX via __fastcall)\n- nY (int): Y starting position in pixels (EDX via __fastcall)\n- nMinVal (int): Minimum allowed pixel width for rendering\n- nMaxVal (int): Maximum allowed pixel width (-1 = unlimited)\n- nRenderOffset (int): Render offset for conditional drawing\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- nMaxVal < 0: Function returns immediately without rendering\n- nStrLen <= 0: No iteration occurs\n- Cel mode == 6: Skip glyph rendering (direct mode)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xFF: Escape sequence indicator\n- 0x0A: Newline character (ASCII LF)\n- 0x100: ASCII boundary check\n- 0x12 (18): Number of DWORDs in CEL cache\n- 5: Drawing mode constant for GfxInterface calls\n- 10: Line height divisor\n\nCalled Functions:\n- GetWindowMode(): Returns current window/render mode\n- Unicode::strlen (g_pfnstrlen): Get Unicode string length  \n- Unicode::strnicmp: Compare escape code characters\n- GetCelDataByIndex: Lookup CEL glyph data\n- GetCelModeValue: Get render mode value\n- GfxInterfaceCall84: Render animated CEL frame\n- GfxInterface_DrawConditional: Conditional glyph rendering",
