      "name": "CreateTextListWidget",
      "signature": "int * CreateTextListWidget(dword dwType, dword dwData, Unicode * pString, int nWidth, int * pnParam5, int * pnParam6)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int *",
      "comment": "Creates and initializes a text list widget with Unicode entries.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x6c-byte widget structure and zero-initialize\n2. Set type to 7, apply bitmasks from gdwBitMasks_exref\n3. Store Unicode string, width, dimension index\n4. Initialize event handler function pointers\n5. If pnParam5 has entries, iterate and build text list:\n   - Allocate 0x224-byte text item per entry\n   - Validate string ID and copy Unicode text (max 255 chars)\n   - Track maximum text width across all entries\n   - Link items into linked list at offset 0x220\n6. Set active font and link object to global list\n\nParameters:\n- dwType (ECX): Widget type identifier\n- dwData (EDX): Widget-specific data value\n- pString: Unicode string for widget header\n- nWidth: Base width in pixels\n- pnParam5: Array count ptr; if non-zero, pnParam5+1 is entry array\n- pnParam6: Index into g_adDimensionTable\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to initialized widget structure, never NULL\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x6c (108): Widget structure size\n- 0x224 (548): Text item structure size\n- 0x220 (544): Linked list next pointer offset\n- 0x1b (27): DWORD count for zeroing (27*4=108)\n- 0xff (255): Max Unicode string length",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:aa4809979ca20bc5b1533077a0214696a03011bf5229ffc010494e4346d4b964",
