      "name": "CaptureScreenshot",
      "signature": "undefined CaptureScreenshot(undefined4 param_1, undefined4 param_2, DWORD param_3)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Captures the current screen to a JPEG file with throttling support.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x4F50 bytes of stack space for local buffers\n2. Get current tick count and compare with last capture time\n3. If less than 1000ms (0x3E8) since last capture, skip (throttle)\n4. Query graphics interface for screen dimensions (width x height)\n5. Allocate pixel buffer sized for RGB24 (width * height * 3 bytes)\n6. Call GfxInterface method 0x28 to capture screen pixels to buffer\n7. If capture fails, jump to cleanup\n8. Format output filename using counter from g_dwScreenshotIndex\n9. Attempt to create output file; if exists, increment counter and retry\n10. Initialize Intel JPEG Library structure (0x1390 bytes zeroed)\n11. Configure JPEG parameters: dimensions, quality=100 (0x64), source format\n12. Call ijlWrite to compress and save JPEG\n13. Call ijlFree to release JPEG resources\n14. Release pixel buffer allocation\n15. Update g_dwLastCaptureTime with current tick count\n\nParameters:\n  pbPath (byte*): Base path/prefix for screenshot filename\n  nWidth (int): Requested output width (used for buffer sizing)\n  dwFlags (uint): Capture flags (reserved, currently unused)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; failure handled silently\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns early if called within 1000ms of last capture (throttling)\n  - Automatically increments filename counter on file collision\n  - Silently fails if screen capture or file creation fails\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x4F50 - Stack allocation for local buffers and JPEG structure\n  0x3E8 (1000) - Minimum milliseconds between captures (throttle)\n  0x665 (1637) - FogMemAlloc allocation type for pixel buffer\n  0x677 (1655) - ReleasePoolAllocation type for pixel buffer\n  0x1390 (5008) - Size of Intel JPEG Library structure\n  0x64 (100) - JPEG quality percentage\n  0x80 - CreateFile dwDesiredAccess (GENERIC_WRITE)\n  0x3 - CreateFile dwCreationDisposition (OPEN_EXISTING)\n\nStructure Layout - JPEG_CORE_PROPERTIES (at ESP+0x11C):\n  Offset  Size  Field              Type    Description\n  0x00    0x04  dwSize             uint    Structure size (0x1390)\n  0x10    0x04  nWidth             int     Image width in pixels\n  0x14    0x04  nHeight            int     Image height in pixels\n  0x0C    0x04  pbDIBBytes         byte*   Pointer to pixel buffer\n  0x20    0x04  nDIBChannels       int     Source channels (1=RGB24)\n  0x28    0x04  pbJFIFFile         byte*   Output filename pointer\n  0x34    0x04  nJFIFWidth         int     JPEG output width\n  0x38    0x04  nJFIFHeight        int     JPEG output height\n  0x58    0x04  nJPGQuality        int     JPEG quality (0x64=100%)\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n  g_dwLastCaptureTime (0x6F961564): Last capture tick for throttling\n  g_dwScreenshotIndex (0x6F921554): Auto-incrementing filename counter",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.09d",
