      "name": "GetDataTableEntry",
      "signature": "void * GetDataTableEntry(int nIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Returns pointer to indexed entry in data table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Shift index left by 8 bits (multiply by 256) to convert array index to 64-byte offset (256 >> 2 = 64)\n2. Add base address of data table (0x6f9c5994)\n3. Return computed pointer\n\nParameters:\n- nIndex (int): Zero-based array index\n\nReturns:\n- void *: Pointer to the indexed entry in the data table. Each entry is 64 bytes apart.\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x8: Left shift amount (multiply index by 256, which equals 64 * 4 for 32-bit pointer arithmetic)\n- 0x40 (64): Entry stride in bytes",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
