      "name": "ProcessItemArray",
      "signature": "void ProcessItemArray(int nContext, int nItems, int nCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Processes array of items, calling ordinal function for each element.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify context pointer is not NULL (assert if NULL)\n2. If count is 0, return early\n3. Iterate through item array with 3-element stride\n4. For each item, call Ordinal_10021 with element values at offsets -4, 0, +4\n5. Decrement count and continue until all items processed\n\nParameters:\n- nContext: Context/object pointer (verified non-NULL)\n- pdwItems: Pointer to item array (points to first element after -4 offset)\n- nCount: Number of items to process\n\nReturns:\n- void (assertion on NULL context, else returns normally)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:feda3f3053d7eda381dc9663085e59fe402d2ec3d4255df12adb20c2d95f663a",
