      "name": "LeaveCriticalSectionEx",
      "signature": "dword LeaveCriticalSectionEx(dword hLock, dword dwResourceId, dword dwContext, int nIgnoreError)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Synchronization wrapper: Release critical section with fallback error handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10102 (Fog.LeaveCriticalSection) to release thread lock\n2. Test result: if zero (failure), jump to step 3; else return success (1)\n3. Call GetLastError to retrieve Windows error code\n4. Check nIgnoreError flag: if non-zero (suppress), return failure (0)\n5. Check if error is ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND (0x2): if yes, return failure\n6. Otherwise call Ordinal_10026 (Fog.ErrorMsg) with error context\n7. Call FUN_6fb9a10f(-1) to terminate (non-returning)\n\nParameters:\n- hLock (dword): Critical section handle (IMPLICIT in ECX via __fastcall)\n- dwResourceId (dword): Resource identifier for error logging\n- dwContext (dword): Additional context/flags\n- nIgnoreError (int): Suppress error handling if non-zero\n\nReturns:\n- 1 if critical section successfully released\n- 0 if release failed or error suppressed\n- Function may not return on unhandled error (calls exit)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04b",
