      "name": "ReadFileAsyncWithValidation",
      "signature": "void ReadFileAsyncWithValidation(uint dwFileHandle, int nFile, int * pBytesRead, int nBytesToRead)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Reads file asynchronously and validates the operation completed correctly.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate file handle is non-zero\n2. Call ReadFileAsync to initiate async read operation\n3. Validate read operation succeeded via GetKeyValue\n4. Verify bytes read matches expected byte count\n\nParameters:\n- hFile (uint): File handle to read from\n- nBytesToRead (int): Number of bytes requested\n- pBuffer (void*): Buffer to read data into\n- nExpectedBytes (int): Expected byte count for validation\n\nReturns:\n- void; asserts on failure via FUN_6f9e5965\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x104 (260): Local buffer size for GetKeyValue call\n- 0x87, 0x8f, 0x92: Assert line numbers",
