      "name": "AdjustValueWithBitOps",
      "signature": "int AdjustValueWithBitOps(ExtendedFloat * pInputFloat, uint * pOutputData, ConversionConfig * pConfig)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Converts extended precision floating-point number to target precision format\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract exponent and sign from input extended float structure\n2. Load mantissa components (low, mid, high) into local variables  \n3. Check for zero exponent (special case: -0x3FFF indicates zero/denormalized)\n4. If zero exponent, test mantissa for actual zero using CheckArrayFirstThreeZero\n5. If true zero, set result code to 0 and clear mantissa components\n6. For normal numbers, backup mantissa using CopyThreeIntegers\n7. Clear high bits and truncate using ClearBitAndTruncateHigh based on precision\n8. Adjust exponent if truncation occurred (increment by 1)\n9. Check exponent bounds against config limits (min/max exponent range)\n10. Handle underflow: clear mantissa if exponent below minimum range\n11. Handle overflow: set infinity bit (0x80000000) if exponent exceeds maximum\n12. For in-range values, restore mantissa and apply precision shifts\n13. Combine adjusted exponent, sign bit, and mantissa into output word\n14. Store result in 32-bit or 64-bit format based on output configuration\n\nParameters:\npInputFloat - Pointer to ExtendedFloat structure containing 12-byte extended precision value\npOutputData - Pointer to output buffer for converted floating-point data  \npConfig - Pointer to ConversionConfig structure with precision and range parameters\n\nReturns:\n0 - Input was zero or resulted in zero after conversion\n1 - Overflow occurred, result is infinity \n2 - Normal conversion completed successfully\n\nStructure Layout:\nExtendedFloat (12 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name           Type    Description\n0x00    2     wMantissaLow        ushort  Low 16 bits of mantissa\n0x02    4     dwMantissaMid       uint    Middle 32 bits of mantissa  \n0x06    4     dwMantissaHigh      uint    High 32 bits of mantissa\n0x0A    2     wExponentAndSign    ushort  Exponent (bits 0-14) and sign (bit 15)\n\nConversionConfig (24 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name           Type    Description\n0x00    4     dwMaxExponent       uint    Maximum allowed exponent value\n0x04    4     dwNormalizedExponent uint   Exponent for normalized range  \n0x08    4     dwPrecisionBits     uint    Number of precision bits to maintain\n0x0C    4     dwMantissaBits      uint    Mantissa bit width for shifts\n0x10    4     dwOutputBits        uint    Output format (0x20=32-bit, 0x40=64-bit)\n0x14    4     dwExponentBias      uint    Bias value added to final exponent\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic number 0x3FFF: Extended precision exponent bias\n- Magic number 0x7FFF: Exponent mask (excludes sign bit)  \n- Magic number 0x8000: Sign bit mask in exponent field\n- Magic number 0x80000000: Infinity/overflow indicator in mantissa\n- Magic number 0x1F: Shift mask for mantissa bit positioning",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:0463e45e494f67c33b3c8dec1837b08bcdb9fbeb802ce9786572c2430726ec4c",
