      "name": "AllocateStreamPropertyTableSlot",
      "signature": "dword AllocateStreamPropertyTableSlot(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Allocate and initialize next available stream property table slot with thread synchronization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire global critical section 0x12 (main lock) for exclusive access\n2. Search existing property table array (g_pStreamPropertyTables) for unused slot:\n   - Iterate through table slots; each slot array holds 32 entries of 0x24 bytes\n   - For each uninitialized entry (byte[1] & 0x01 == 0):\n     - Double-check with critical section 0x11 if entry uninitialized\n     - Initialize critical section at offset 0x0c within entry\n     - Enter initialized critical section and mark entry as used (byte[1] |= 0x01)\n     - Set entry ID to -1 (0xffffffff) and return slot index (table_index * 32 + entry_offset / 0x24)\n3. If all existing tables exhausted, allocate new 0x480-byte table:\n   - Allocate memory, increment g_dwMaxEntityCount by 0x20 (32 slots)\n   - Initialize all 32 entries (byte[1]=0, entry_id=0xffffffff, refcount=0, byte[5]=0x0a)\n   - Call FUN_6fba2456(slot_index << 5) to register new table\n   - Return computed slot index (table_index << 5)\n4. Release global critical section 0x12 and return slot index or -1 if failure\n\nParameters:\n  (none)\n\nReturns:\n  EDI: Slot index (0-based) if successful, 0xffffffff (-1) if all slots exhausted\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Entry format: 4 dwords (size 0x24) per slot\n    - [0x00]: Entry ID (set to 0xffffffff when available)\n    - [0x04]: Flags (bit 0x01 = initialized)\n    - [0x08]: Refcount/State\n    - [0x0c..0x18]: CRITICAL_SECTION (16 bytes)\n  - Table array at g_pStreamPropertyTables is array of pointers, max 64 tables\n  - Each table holds max 32 slots (0x480 bytes / 0x24 per slot)\n  - Critical section 0x12: Main stream lock\n  - Critical section 0x11: Initialization race condition guard\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x480: Table allocation size (1152 bytes = 32 slots * 0x24)\n  0x120: Search boundary (32 * 0x09 - offset adjustment for loop increment)\n  0x24: Slot size in bytes (36 bytes per entry)\n  0x09: Loop increment in dwords (0x24 bytes = 9 dwords)\n  0x20: Slots per table allocation (32)\n  0x0c: Critical section offset within slot\n  0x05: Flag byte offset\n  0x0a: Magic marker (0x0a = 10)\n  0x01: Initialized flag bit\n  0xffffffff: Available entry marker (-1)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
