      "name": "BuildLocaleString",
      "signature": "char * BuildLocaleString(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Builds composite locale string by comparing current and stored locale category values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Allocate buffer if not exists (0x351 = 849 bytes)\n  2. Initialize buffer with first locale category entry (LC_COLLATE)\n  3. Loop through 5 locale categories (LC_COLLATE through LC_CTYPE):\n     a. Append semicolon separator to buffer\n     b. Compare current category value with stored value\n     c. Track if any mismatch found (fAllMatch flag)\n     d. Append category name, equals sign, and value to buffer\n  4. If all categories match: free buffer and return default locale pointer\n  5. If any mismatch: return constructed locale string buffer\n\nParameters:\n  (none) - Function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\n  char* - Pointer to locale string buffer if categories differ\n  char* - Pointer to default locale string (g_pszDefaultLocale) if all match\n\nStructure Layout (g_aLocaleCategoryTable at 0x4129e8):\n  Offset | Size | Field         | Type   | Description\n  0x00   | 4    | pszCurrent    | char*  | Current category value pointer\n  0x04   | 4    | pszCatName    | char*  | Category name string (LC_*)\n  0x08   | 4    | pszStored     | char*  | Stored/reference value pointer\n  (Entry size: 0x0C bytes, 5 entries total)",
