      "name": "ConvertNumberToString",
      "signature": "char * ConvertNumberToString(int nValue, int nValueHigh, char * szBuffer, dword dwRadix)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Wrapper for converting a signed 64-bit number to string representation in specified radix.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize nNegativeFlag to 0\n2. Check if dwRadix == 10 (decimal) AND nValueHigh < 1 AND nValueHigh < 0\n3. If all conditions true (negative 64-bit number in decimal radix), set nNegativeFlag = 1\n4. Call Int64ToStringWithRadix() with computed nNegativeFlag and buffer\n5. Return szBuffer pointer\n\nParameters:\nnValue - Low 32-bits of signed 64-bit number to convert\nnValueHigh - High 32-bits of signed 64-bit number (sign extension/indicator)\nszBuffer - Pointer to destination buffer for output string\ndwRadix - Base for conversion (typically 10 for decimal, 16 for hex)\n\nReturns:\nszBuffer - Returns input buffer pointer unchanged (allows function chaining)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nNegative detection: Requires radix 10 AND nValueHigh < 1 AND nValueHigh < 0\nOnly sets flag for negative detection in decimal mode\nUnsigned conversions pass flag=0 for positive behavior\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Int64ToStringWithRadix() - Performs actual number-to-string conversion",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
