      "comment": "Reallocates a memory block with multi-strategy fallback.\n\nAttempts reallocation using a managed descriptor system first, then falls back\nto Windows Heap APIs if the managed system fails. Supports callback-driven\nretry for out-of-memory conditions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If pSourceBlock is NULL, behaves like malloc(dwNewSize).\n2. If dwNewSize is 0, frees pSourceBlock and returns NULL.\n3. Acquire critical section (index 9) for thread safety.\n4. Find memory descriptor for pSourceBlock via FindMemoryDescriptorByAddress.\n5. If new size fits managed threshold (g_dwManagedHeapThreshold):\n   a. Try in-place resize via ProcessHeapFreeBlock.\n   b. If fails, allocate new block via AllocateMemoryDescriptorBlock.\n   c. Copy data using OptimizedMemoryMove (min of old/new size).\n   d. Free old block via FreeMemoryBlockWithLinkedListCleanup.\n6. If managed allocation fails, fall back to HeapAlloc/HeapReAlloc.\n7. Align size to 16-byte boundary before heap operations.\n8. If allocation fails and callback handler exists (g_pAllocationCallback),\n   invoke InvokeCallbackHandler and retry from step 5.\n9. Release critical section and return result.\n\nParameters:\n  pSourceBlock - Pointer to existing memory block to reallocate, or NULL for new allocation.\n  dwNewSize    - Requested new size in bytes. Zero frees the block.\n\nReturns:\n  void* - Pointer to reallocated block on success.\n          NULL if dwNewSize is 0 (block freed).\n          NULL if allocation fails after all retry strategies exhausted.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL pSourceBlock: Equivalent to malloc(dwNewSize).\n  - Zero dwNewSize: Frees pSourceBlock, returns NULL.\n  - Size alignment: All heap allocations aligned to 16 bytes.\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  - 0x9: Critical section index for memory manager.\n  - 0xFFFFFFE0 (-32): Maximum valid allocation size check.\n  - 0x0F/0xFFFFFFF0: 16-byte alignment mask.\n\nError Handling:\n  - Returns NULL on allocation failure.\n  - Attempts callback-driven retry if g_pAllocationCallback is set.\n  - Original block preserved if reallocation fails (no data loss).",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
