      "name": "EditBoxProcessClipboardInput",
      "signature": "int EditBoxProcessClipboardInput(void * pEditData, Unicode nCharMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Processes clipboard input operations for an edit box control.\n\nHandles standard clipboard keyboard shortcuts:\n- Ctrl+V (0x16): Paste text from clipboard into edit box\n- Ctrl+C (0x03): Copy selected text to clipboard  \n- Ctrl+X (0x18): Cut selected text to clipboard\n- Ctrl+A (0x01): Select all text in edit box\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pEditData pointer is not NULL (FogAssert on failure)\n2. Verify EditData structure integrity (first DWORD must be 1)\n3. Check if character mode is valid for the current edit box flags\n4. For Tab (0x09) with callback: invoke custom tab handler callback\n5. Call CheckBitFlagIndex to validate character mode against allowed modes\n6. Process command based on bCharMode value:\n   - 0x16 (Ctrl+V): Open clipboard, get CF_TEXT data, validate and insert\n   - 0x03 (Ctrl+C): Copy selection to clipboard using GlobalAlloc/GlobalLock\n   - 0x18 (Ctrl+X): Copy selection then delete (SwapEditBoxSelection)\n   - 0x01 (Ctrl+A): Set selection start=0, end=text length\n   - 0x0D (Enter): Insert newline if multiline flag set\n   - Other: Insert character at cursor position\n7. Convert between Unicode and ANSI using win2Unicode/unicode2Win\n8. Validate text fits within max length (EditData+0x48)\n9. Update cursor position and selection state (EditData+0x54, +0x58)\n10. Call EditBoxValidateInsert to finalize and trigger change callback\n\nParameters:\n  pEditData (ECX) - Pointer to EditData structure containing edit box state\n  bCharMode (DL) - Character/command code to process (keyboard input)\n\nReturns:\n  1 on success (text modified or selection changed)\n  0 on failure (validation failed, clipboard error, or no-op)\n\nEditData Structure Layout (relevant offsets):\n  +0x00: dwMagic - Validation marker (must be 1)\n  +0x08: dwInputFlags - Allowed input types bitmask\n  +0x10: nHeight - Control height\n  +0x14: nWidth - Control width  \n  +0x18: nPaddingY - Vertical padding\n  +0x40: nMarginLeft - Left margin\n  +0x44: nMarginRight - Right margin\n  +0x48: nMaxLength - Maximum text buffer length\n  +0x54: nSelectionStart - Selection start index (-1 if no selection)\n  +0x58: nSelectionEnd - Selection end index\n  +0x5C: wszTextBuffer - Wide character text buffer (Unicode)\n  +0x25C: nCursorPosition - Current cursor position in text\n  +0x260: dwEditFlags - Edit mode flags (0x04=tab callback, 0x08=multiline, 0x10=special, 0x20=limited charset)\n  +0x268: pfnCallback - Optional input validation callback\n  +0x26C: pfnChangeCallback - Text changed notification callback\n  +0x270: nFontIndex - Active font index\n\nFlag Bits (EditData+0x260):\n  0x04 - Has tab callback handler\n  0x08 - Multiline mode (allows Enter key)\n  0x10 - Special character mode\n  0x20 - Limited character set mode\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x200 (512) - Unicode text buffer element count\n  0x100 (256) - Temporary buffer size\n  0x2000 - GlobalAlloc flags (GMEM_MOVEABLE)\n  0xBBC (3004) - Stack frame size for local buffers",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04b",
