      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Processes keyboard input for edit box control, handling text insertion, deletion, navigation,\nselection, and callback invocation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input: Ensure pEditBox is non-null and type==1\n2. Check enabled state: Verify edit box is enabled via gdwBitMasks_exref flags\n3. Calculate text pointer: pEditBox + pEditBox[0x97]*2 + 0x5C (text buffer)\n4. Handle key by type:\n   - Backspace/Delete: Remove selection or preceding character\n   - Tab: Navigate to next/previous sibling edit box\n   - Enter: Invoke user callback or close if not multi-line\n   - Escape: Invoke close callback\n   - Navigation (Home/End/PgUp/PgDn): Move cursor\n   - Arrow keys: Adjust selection or cursor position\n5. Update cursor offset (pEditBox[0x97]) relative to text pointer\n6. Call OnChange callback if text was modified (nEdited==1)\n7. Return 1 if handled (or multi-line+Enter), 0 if should propagate\n\nParameters:\n- pEditBox (int*): Edit box structure [ECX], contains:\n  - [0x0]: Type (must be 1)\n  - [0x2]: Flags (validated against gdwBitMasks_exref)\n  - [0x54]: Selection start (cursor position, -1=none)\n  - [0x58]: Selection end\n  - [0x97]: Text offset (in Unicode chars, offset from base)\n  - [0x98]: Edit flags (0x8=accept special chars like +)\n  - [0x99]: OnChange callback (called after text change)\n  - [0x9A]: OnValidate callback (returns 0 to reject key)\n  - [0x9B]: OnClose callback\n  - [0x9E]: Previous sibling pointer\n  - [0x9F]: Next sibling pointer\n  - [0x25C]: Text length or offset (variable usage)\n- cKeyCode (char [DL]): Keyboard character code\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Key handled successfully, edit box updated or callback invoked\n- 0: Key rejected or invalid state (non-multi-line + non-special-key)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Backspace (0x08): Delete selection or previous char; block if no selection+cursor==0\n- Delete (0x2E): Delete selection or next char\n- Tab (0x09): Tab key with Shift traverses prev/next edit boxes\n- Enter (0x0D): Invoke OnChange callback; return based on (flags & 0x2)\n- Escape (0x1B): Invoke OnClose callback, always return 1\n- Shift+Arrows: Extend selection; plain arrows move cursor only\n\nAssembly Notes:\n- unaff_EDI (szTextBuffer): Preserved EDI register from caller, points to text buffer\n  for Unicode::strlen calls. Cannot be renamed via decompiler (assembly-only).",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04b",
