      "comment": "Renders the composite text label for a game unit on screen.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate unit pointer is not null (assert on failure)\n2. Check if unit display flags permit rendering\n3. Calculate vertical offset based on unit type (NPC=+6, special=+15)\n4. Determine rendering mode based on unit type (0x12=special, 0x10=player)\n5. Initialize display text buffer (512 wide chars)\n6. Copy unit name from appropriate offset based on type\n7. For players, also fetch and append title string\n8. Set active font to size 12 for rendering\n9. Convert unicode to ANSI, measure width, apply ellipsis if >120px\n10. Calculate centered X position from text width\n11. Render first pass if special mode enabled (title)\n12. Render final text with color at calculated position\n\nParameters:\npUnit (ECX) - Pointer to unit structure containing display data\n\nReturns:\nint - 1 on successful render, 0 if unit filtered or null\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Unit type 0x12: Special rendering mode 3 with title offset\n- Unit type 0x10: Player rendering mode 3 with title\n- Magic values D2DV, D2ST, D2XP: Use alternate name offset 0x14c\n- Text truncation at 120 pixels with ellipsis appended\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x12: NPC/monster unit type\n- 0x10: Player unit type\n- 0xCC: Standard name field offset\n- 0x14C: Alternate name field offset\n- 0x1CC: Title string offset\n- 0x230: Unit signature field offset\n- D2DV (0x44324456): Diablo 2 Vanilla signature\n- D2ST (0x44325354): Diablo 2 Stash signature\n- D2XP (0x44325850): Diablo 2 Expansion signature\n\nStructure Layout (Unit at pUnit):\nOffset  Size  Field           Type        Description\n0x00    4     dwFlags         uint        Display control flags\n0x14    4     nScreenY        int         Screen Y position\n0x18    4     nSlotY          int         Slot vertical offset\n0x1C    4     nUnitType       uint        Type identifier (0x10=player, 0x12=NPC)\n0xCC    N     szName          char[]      Primary name string (ANSI)\n0x14C   N     szAltName       char[]      Alternate name string (ANSI)\n0x1CC   N     szTitle         wchar_t[]   Character title (unicode)\n0x230   4     dwSignature     uint        Unit type signature magic",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.09d",
