      "name": "CreateGameObjectByType",
      "signature": "dword * CreateGameObjectByType(int nObjectType, int nXPosition, int nYPosition, int nParameter, dword dwFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "dword *",
      "comment": "Creates and initializes a game object by type, allocating memory and setting initial state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x150 (336) bytes of memory for object structure\n2. Initialize all allocated memory to zero using REP STOSD loop\n3. Set object type field to 9 in allocated structure\n4. Apply global bit masks to object flags from gdwBitMasks_exref\n5. Initialize object dimension fields with calculated X and Y offsets\n6. Store input parameters into object fields for later use\n7. Link initialized object to active object list via LinkObjectToList\n8. Return pointer to newly allocated and initialized object\n\nParameters:\n- nObjectType (int in ECX): Type identifier for object being created\n- nXPosition (int in EDX): X-coordinate for object positioning\n- nYPosition (int on stack): Y-coordinate for object positioning\n- nParameter (int on stack): Additional initialization parameter value\n- dwFlags (dword on stack): Creation flags for object initialization\n\nReturns:\n- dword *: Pointer to allocated object structure; never returns NULL\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x150 (336): Total allocated object size in bytes\n- 0x54 (84): Number of dwords to zero (336/4 = 84)\n- 0x1d4 (468): X-dimension offset constant\n- 0x3c (60): Y-dimension offset constant",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.09d",
