      "name": "InitItemTypesAndComponents",
      "signature": "void InitItemTypesAndComponents(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes item type tables and component mappings for the game's item system.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check initialization guard at 0x6f96094c; exit early if already initialized\n2. Set guard flag to 1 to prevent re-initialization\n3. Load item Excel tables via LoadItemTypesTable and LoadItemExcelTables\n4. Clear the component mapping table at 0x6f924be0 (0x2fd entries using REP STOSD)\n5. Initialize 31 component entry structures on stack with:\n   - Ptr: Pointer to component data table\n   - Count: Number of entries (0xA=10, 0xB=11, 0xD=13, etc.)\n   - Flag1/Flag2: Component type flags\n   - TypePtr: Pointer to type definition\n6. Load Excel table data and allocate 0xEC byte buffer for processing\n7. Initialize armor type strings: \"lit \", \"med \", \"hvy \" at mapping slots 0-2\n8. Iterate through all item records in the item table:\n   a. Get component type byte at record offset 0x26\n   b. Check if item is armor type (types 0x2D, 0x03, 0x02, 0x25)\n   c. Skip if item matches existing mapping or is not armor\n   d. Search for free slot in mapping table (max 0xFF slots)\n   e. Assign item type to slot with type code and variant lookup\n9. Store max slot index (0xFF) at 0x6f9608f4\n\nParameters:\n  None (void function)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Initializes global item type tables\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Early exit if guard flag already set (prevents double init)\n  - Slot index clamped to 0xFF maximum\n  - Armor type classification uses IsItemTypeEquivalent checks\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x6f96094c - Initialization guard flag\n  0x6f924be0 - Component mapping table base (12 bytes per entry)\n  0x2fd (765) - Number of mapping table entries\n  0x250 (592) - Item record size in bytes\n  0x26 - Offset to component type byte in item record\n  0x84/0x80 - Alternate type field offsets\n  0x8c - Variant lookup field offset\n  0x2D/0x32 - Armor type constants\n  0xEC (236) - Processing buffer size\n\nStructure Layout (Component Entry - 20 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field      Type  Description\n  0x00    4     Ptr        uint  Component data pointer\n  0x04    4     Count      uint  Entry count\n  0x08    4     Flag1      uint  Primary type flag\n  0x0C    4     Flag2      uint  Secondary type flag\n  0x10    4     TypePtr    uint  Type definition pointer",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:56bba06b414f33a003ef27ef1d97fc8c",
