      "name": "ProcessEditBoxMessage",
      "signature": "void ProcessEditBoxMessage(EditData * pEditData, uint dwMessage)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Processes window messages for edit box controls (WM_LBUTTONDOWN, WM_KEYDOWN, etc).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate edit box structure type and state flags\n2. Calculate visible text bounds based on screen dimensions and control position\n3. Determine if cursor position is within valid text area (fInBounds)\n4. Check for double-click (time < 300ms) on same control for fast selection\n5. Handle shift+click for text selection or cursor movement by character\n6. Process keyboard input (GetKeyState for shift modifier)\n7. Invoke control callback function if defined\n8. Cache last edited control and tick count for double-click detection\n\nParameters:\n- pEditData (EditData*): Pointer to edit box data structure containing position, size, text buffer, cursor state\n- dwMessage (uint): Message type (0x201 = WM_LBUTTONDOWN, others from Windows API)\n\nReturns:\n- Result from control callback (if defined), 0 if no callback\n\nStructure Layout (EditData offsets):\nOffset  Size  Field          Type      Description\n0x00    4     eType          int       Control type (1 = EDITBOX)\n0x08    4     dwFlags        uint      State and capability flags\n0x0C    4     nY             int       Y position\n0x10    4     nLineHeight    int       Height of single text line\n0x14    4     nHeight        int       Total control height\n0x18    4     nWidth         int       Control width\n0x34    4     pfnCallback    code*     Callback function pointer\n0x40    4     nLineOffset    int       Line height offset\n0x44    4     nVertOffset    int       Vertical offset\n0x4C    4     nCursorPos     int       Character position in text\n0x54    4     nSelStart      int       Selection start (-1 if none)\n0x58    4     nSelEnd        int       Selection end position\n0x5C    N     szTextBuffer   wchar[]   Unicode text buffer\n0x25C   4     dwCursorX      uint      Pixel X position from line start\n0x270   4     hFont          handle    Active font handle\n0x280   4     dwDragState    uint      Mouse drag state (1 = dragging)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x201: WM_LBUTTONDOWN message\n- 300: Double-click threshold in milliseconds\n- 0x10: VK_SHIFT virtual key code\n- 0x8000: High bit mask for key state check\n\nError Handling:\n- Asserts if pEditData is NULL (line 0x6d0)\n- Asserts if eType != 1 (not an edit box, line 0x6d1)\n- Early return if control is disabled or invisible (flag bits 0, 8)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:0872ee047e1abd4d5a5105033bdeeb4ce704baf7f11fc03d61eb9b8303da7092",
