      "name": "RenderUnicodeStringWithOverlay",
      "signature": "void RenderUnicodeStringWithOverlay(ushort * pString, uint param_2, int nY, int nOpacity, int nAlignment, int param_6)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Renders a Unicode string with text sizing, line breaks, and optional color overlay.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate string is non-empty and calculate display width\n2. Count line breaks (0x0A) to determine number of lines\n3. Query current font metrics (height and scale factor)\n4. Determine horizontal offset based on alignment parameter:\n   - If nAlignment=1, center text (nX - width/2)\n5. Query color overlay values from Ordinal_10041\n6. Clamp X offset to valid range [0, max), apply minimum constraints\n7. If nOpacity=0, render background rectangle\n8. If nOpacity\u22600, scale color fill width by opacity (multiply, shift right 7 bits)\n9. Render background rectangle for remaining non-colored portion\n10. Render the Unicode string with calculated dimensions and colors\n\nParameters:\n- pString (Unicode*): Unicode string to render\n- nX (uint): Horizontal position\n- nY (int): Vertical position\n- nOpacity (int): Color overlay opacity (0=no color, 1-128=varying transparency)\n- nAlignment (int): Text alignment (1=center, other=left)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x14: Font handle structure stride\n- 0x0A: Line break character (newline)\n- 10: Height scaling divisor\n- 0x1F: Minimum X coordinate offset\n- 0x50: Default color value (80 decimal)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:865784ead1b744bb5e3033b83bae6c3b1a6a4e75fdd9a11c2f767cb9b8f43bf4",
