      "name": "WrapUnicodeText",
      "signature": "int * WrapUnicodeText(Unicode * pwsText, int * pnLineCount, int nMaxWidth)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int *",
      "comment": "Wraps Unicode text to fit within a maximum display width by breaking at word boundaries.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate text length via Unicode::strlen\n2. Check if entire text fits via Ordinal_10123 (width calculator)\n3. If fits, allocate single line node and return\n4. Otherwise, iterate from start finding longest segment that fits width\n5. For each oversized segment, search backwards for line break point\n6. Allocate node for fitting segment and link to previous node\n7. Continue from next segment until entire text is processed\n\nParameters:\n- pwsText (Unicode*): Pointer to Unicode string to wrap\n- pnLineCount (int*): Pointer to receive count of created line nodes\n- nMaxWidth (int): Maximum display width for each line\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to head of linked list of line nodes (int* with [1] as next pointer)\n- NULL if text was empty or allocation failed",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:1fb0fa6f881968474ebccfb2afd6d4726b0971426374842a66ae652f532b2553",
