      "name": "ProcessMouseInputAndFindNearestWidget",
      "signature": "void ProcessMouseInputAndFindNearestWidget(uint dwMouseCoords)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Processes mouse input coordinates and finds the nearest UI widget for interaction.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract mouse X (low word) and Y (high word >> 16) from packed dwMouseCoords+8/+0xc\n2. Calculate scroll division: Y / 0x78 (120 pixels per scroll unit)\n3. Call DispatchVirtualMethod to get screen boundaries, then decrement both by 1\n4. Call Ordinal_10047 (D2gfx.GetVideoMode) to check if cursor adjustment needed\n5. If adjustment needed, clamp mouse X to screen width and Y to screen height, call SetCursorPos\n6. Store clamped coordinates in g_nScreenHeight (X) and g_nScreenWidth (Y) - note reversed naming\n7. Check IsScreenPopupActiveBitSet - if popup active, return immediately\n8. Get starting widget from g_dwLastInventoryItem or g_pInventoryList\n9. Iterate through widget linked list (offset 0x3c = next pointer):\n   a. Check widget type == 5 (scrollbar widget type)\n   b. Verify visibility bits set in gdwBitMasks_exref\n   c. Call GetScrollbarHeight to verify positive height\n   d. Calculate distance from mouse to widget bounds using squared distance formula\n   e. Track nearest widget based on Euclidean distance comparison\n10. If nearest scrollbar found, call ScrollbarAdjustPosition\n11. Otherwise iterate widgets looking for type 6 (button), call OnButtonPressed\n12. Call InsertCacheNodeWithCookie to cache the interaction\n\nParameters:\n  dwMouseCoords - Packed structure containing mouse coordinates at offsets +0x8 and +0xc\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns early if IsScreenPopupActiveBitSet returns non-zero\n  - Widget linked list traversal via offset 0x3c (field index 15)\n  - Distance calculation uses squared values to avoid sqrt\n  - SSA temporaries (iVar3, piVar4, etc.) are decompiler-generated and cannot be renamed\n\nOrdinal References:\n  - Ordinal_10047: D2gfx.GetVideoMode - returns current video mode for cursor boundary check\n\nWidget Structure Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field       Description\n  0x00    4     dwType      Widget type (5=scrollbar, 6=button)\n  0x08    4     dwFlags     Visibility/state flags\n  0x0C    4     nPosY       Widget Y position\n  0x10    4     nPosX       Widget X position\n  0x14    4     nHeight     Widget height\n  0x18    4     nWidth      Widget width\n  0x3C    4     pNext       Next widget in linked list",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
