      "name": "TextBoxMouseToLineIndex",
      "signature": "void TextBoxMouseToLineIndex(int * * ppParams)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts mouse Y position to line index for TextBox UI widget.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Dereference ppParams to get pTextData pointer\n2. Assert pTextData is non-null (assert \"pParams->window\")\n3. Assert pTextData->eType == 4 (D2WIN_TEXTBOX)\n4. Check bit mask at gdwBitMasks[2] against flags - return 0 if not set\n5. Check bit mask at gdwBitMasks[0] against flags - return 0 if not set\n6. Check nLineCount (offset 0x54) >= 1 - return 0 if no lines\n7. Check dwOptions bit 0x1 (offset 0x5C) - skip calculation if not set\n8. Calculate relative Y: nRelativeY = (nY - nX) + g_nScreenWidth\n9. Set active font to pTextData->nFontId (offset 0x94)\n10. Handle CJK languages (7=Japanese, 9=Korean):\n    - Get font height property\n    - If height < 14: g_dwCJKFontHeight = (height > 7) ? 7 : 6\n    - Else: g_dwCJKFontHeight = 8\n11. Calculate line index: (nRelativeY - nHeight) / (fontHeight + g_dwCJKFontHeight) + nScrollOffset\n12. Store result in pTextData->nHoverLine (offset 0x60)\n13. If dwOptions bit 0x8 set: clamp to [0, nLineCount-1]\n14. Else: if out of bounds [0, nLineCount), set to -1\n15. If pMessageHandler (offset 0x34) is null, return 0\n16. Call pMessageHandler(ppParams) and return its result\n\nParameters:\nppParams - Pointer to pointer to TextData structure (stack param)\n\nReturns:\n0 - If validation fails or no message handler\nResult of pMessageHandler callback otherwise\n\nTextData Structure Layout (partial):\nOffset  Size  Field           Description\n0x00    4     eType           Object type (must be 4 for TEXTBOX)\n0x08    4     dwFlags         Bit mask flags\n0x10    4     nX              X position\n0x18    4     nY              Y position\n0x34    4     pMessageHandler Callback function pointer\n0x44    4     nHeight         Widget height\n0x54    4     nLineCount      Total number of lines\n0x58    4     nScrollOffset   Current scroll position\n0x5C    4     dwOptions       Option flags (bit 0x1, 0x8)\n0x60    4     nHoverLine      Calculated hover line index\n0x94    4     nFontId         Active font identifier\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Language 7 (Japanese) and 9 (Korean) use CJK font height adjustment\n- Bit 0x8 in dwOptions enables clamping to valid range instead of -1 for out-of-bounds\n\nDecompiler Notes:\n- extraout_var* variables are CONCAT31 artifacts from byte-to-int extension\n  when GetCurrentFontProperty() returns a byte value - these represent the\n  upper 3 undefined bytes and cannot be renamed",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
