      "name": "CloseAndCleanupDynamicStreams",
      "signature": "int CloseAndCleanupDynamicStreams(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Closes and cleans up dynamically allocated file stream structures.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquires critical section 2 (stream table protection)\n2. Iterates stream table from index 3 to g_dwStreamStructureCount\n3. For each stream entry with non-null FILE pointer:\n   a. If stream has flags 0x83 set (read/write/error), attempts ThreadSafeFileClose\n   b. Increments close counter on successful close\n4. For streams at index 20 (0x14) or higher (dynamically allocated):\n   a. Deletes critical section at offset 0x20 in structure\n   b. Frees the stream structure memory\n   c. Clears the table entry\n5. Releases critical section 2\n6. Returns count of successfully closed streams\n\nParameters:\n  None - This function operates on the global stream table\n\nReturns:\n  int - Number of file streams successfully closed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Indices 0-2 are reserved (stdin, stdout, stderr) - never processed\n  - Indices 3-19 are static streams - closed but not deallocated\n  - Indices 20+ are dynamic streams - fully cleaned up\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x2 - Critical section index for stream table\n  0x3 - First dynamic stream index (skips standard streams)\n  0x14 (20) - First fully dynamic stream (allocated at runtime)\n  0x20 - Offset to CRITICAL_SECTION in stream structure\n  0x83 - File flags mask: _IOREAD | _IOWRT | _IOERR\n\nStructure Layout (Stream Structure at g_pStreamStructureTable[index]):\n  Offset  Size  Field              Type               Description\n  0x00    4     FILE pointer       FILE*              Standard C file handle\n  0x04    28    (reserved)         byte[28]           Unknown/internal state\n  0x20    24    csLock             CRITICAL_SECTION   Per-stream synchronization",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
