      "name": "CountValidLockContextEntities",
      "signature": "int CountValidLockContextEntities(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Counts valid lock context entities by invoking ProcessLockContextEntities in count mode\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push constant 1 (Count Mode) as parameter\n2. Call ProcessLockContextEntities(1) to count successfully validated entities\n3. Clean up stack and return the count\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nint - Count of successfully validated lock context entities (>= 0)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns 0 if lock context table is empty\n- Returns 0 if no entities pass validation\n\nNotes:\n- This is a thin wrapper that hardcodes nProcessMode=1 (Count Mode)\n- Mode 1 iterates all lock context entries and counts successful validations\n- Validation failures are ignored in count mode, only successes are counted\n- Uses __cdecl callee (ProcessLockContextEntities) with __stdcall wrapper",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
