      "name": "AllocateAndOpenArchiveWithRetry",
      "signature": "int * AllocateAndOpenArchiveWithRetry(int nUnused, char * szArchivePath, int nUnused2, int nUnused3, void * pfnRetryCallback)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int *",
      "comment": "Allocates Archive Structure and Opens with Retry Logic\n\nCreates a 0x108-byte archive structure and attempts to open\nthe specified archive file. Supports retry via callback function\nif initial open fails (e.g., for CD-ROM media detection).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x108 bytes via AllocateMemoryWithTracking\n   - Source: ..\\Source\\D2Hell\\SRC\\Archive.cpp line 0x21A\n2. Initialize archive handle to 0\n3. Attempt to open archive via OpenArchiveWithFallback\n4. If open succeeds, return archive pointer\n5. If open fails and callback provided:\n   a. Call pfnRetryCallback (e.g., prompt user for CD)\n   b. If callback returns non-zero, Sleep(100) and retry\n   c. Continue until callback returns 0 or open succeeds\n6. If all retries fail, release allocation and return NULL\n\nParameters:\n  nUnused - Unused parameter (possibly removed feature)\n  szArchivePath - Path to MPQ archive file\n  nUnused2 - Unused parameter\n  nUnused3 - Unused parameter\n  pfnRetryCallback - Callback function for retry logic, or NULL\n\nReturns:\n  int* - Pointer to 0x108-byte archive structure, or NULL on failure\n\nStructure Layout:\n  +0x00: Handle to opened archive (set by OpenArchiveWithFallback)\n  +0x04: Archive data buffer (0x104 bytes)",
