      "name": "UnlinkAndReleaseControl",
      "signature": "undefined4 UnlinkAndReleaseControl(int pControl)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Unlinks a UI Control from the Active Control List\n\nRemoves a control from the main control linked list and\nmoves it to a secondary (released) list. Also clears\nglobal references if the control was focused or selected.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear global references if control matches:\n   - g_dwLastError - Last error control\n   - g_pFocusedControl - Currently focused control\n   - g_dwLastInventoryItem - Last inventory item and its next\n   - g_fErrorHandlingDisabled - Error handling state\n2. If control list is empty (g_pControlListHead == 0), return 0\n3. If control is the list head:\n   a. Update head to pControl->pNext (offset 0x3C)\n   b. Move control to secondary list\n   c. Return 1\n4. Otherwise, traverse the list to find control:\n   a. Walk linked list via pNext pointers at offset 0x3C\n   b. When found, unlink by setting prev->pNext = control->pNext\n   c. Move control to secondary list via LinkControlToSecondaryList\n\nParameters:\n  pControl - Pointer to the UI control structure to unlink\n\nReturns:\n  int - 1 if control was found and unlinked, 0 if list was empty\n\nStructure Offsets:\n  +0x3C: pNext - Pointer to next control in linked list",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.13d",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:cfcafbe951200e02010590a2323c825cd950095f04c6317a7868ad66f8528095",
