      "name": "ConvertFloatToStringComponents",
      "signature": "void ConvertFloatToStringComponents(double floatValue, int precisionControl, int * pResultArray, uint * pConversionBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts a floating-point number into decimal string components.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load XOR canary token (g_dwStackGuardSeed) and XOR with EBP for stack overflow protection\n2. Convert input double precision float to 80-bit extended precision using ___dtold\n3. Decompose extended float to decimal components using ConvertFloatingPointToDecimalString with precision 0x11 (17 digits)\n4. Store sign byte to result array offset +8 (stored in low byte of int)\n5. Store sign character as signed int to result array offset +0\n6. Store exponent value as signed int to result array offset +4\n7. Copy digit buffer using CopyString to result array + offset\n8. Store buffer pointer to result array offset +0xC\n9. Verify stack canary before return using VerifyStackCanary\n\nParameters:\n  floatValue (double): The floating-point number to convert\n  precisionControl (int): Precision/formatting control value\n  pResultArray (int*): Pointer to int array [4] for results:\n    [+0] = sign character, [+4] = exponent, [+8] = sign byte, [+C] = buffer ptr\n  pConversionBuffer (uint*): Workspace buffer for conversion state\n\nReturns:\n  void - Results written directly to pResultArray\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Stack canary enabled: XOR check verifies stack integrity\n  - Extended precision: 80-bit representation ensures accuracy\n  - Precision constant: 0x11 (17) decimal digits",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.12a",
