      "name": "ProcessEventHandler",
      "signature": "void ProcessEventHandler(EventHandler * pEventHandler)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Processes event handler callbacks for enter/exit event transitions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read event type flag from pEventHandler+0x8 (4 bytes) and store in global DAT_6f8ffba8\n2. If event type is non-zero (enter event):\n   a. Call Ordinal_10039 to check if initialization needed\n   b. If initialization needed (returns 0):\n      - Call Ordinal_10059(0) to configure mode\n      - Set global DAT_6f9a9e28 = 1 (event active flag)\n      - Store current tick count in _DAT_6f9a9e2c via GetTickCount\n      - Set DAT_6f921630 = 2 (state transition)\n      - Set DAT_6f8ffd44 = 1 (processing flag)\n      - Call Ordinal_10061(&DAT_6f922338) to register callback\n   c. Call Ordinal_10004 to process event\n   d. Clear DAT_6f9a9cfc = 0 (reset event flag)\n3. If event type is zero (exit event):\n   a. Check if DAT_6f9a9cfc is zero\n   b. If zero, call Ordinal_10011 and store result in DAT_6f9a9cf8\n   c. Set DAT_6f9a9cfc = 1 (mark event processed)\n   d. If DAT_6f901498 != 1, call Ordinal_10059(1) to reconfigure mode\n4. Call Ordinal_10063 to check post-processing needed\n5. If post-processing needed, call Ordinal_10043 to execute\n6. Clear pEventHandler+0x18 = 0 (reset result field)\n\nParameters:\n  pEventHandler - EventHandler* - Pointer to event handler structure\n    +0x8: Event type flag (0=exit, non-zero=enter)\n    +0x18: Result field (cleared at end)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - DAT_6f8ffba8: Global event type indicator (0 or 1)\n  - DAT_6f9a9cfc: Event processed flag\n  - DAT_6f9a9cf8: Stored result from Ordinal_10011\n  - DAT_6f9a9e28: Event active flag (1=active)\n  - DAT_6f921630: State machine value (2=processing)\n  - DAT_6f8ffd44: Processing active flag (1=active)\n  - DAT_6f901498: Mode configuration flag\n  - GetTickCount: Win32 API for timestamp in milliseconds",
