      "name": "FindLastCharacter",
      "signature": "char * FindLastCharacter(char * pString, int searchChar)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Finds the last occurrence of a character in a null-terminated string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize ECX to -1 and set up EDI with string pointer\n2. Use REPNE SCASB to scan forward until null terminator found, calculating string length\n3. Calculate string length from ECX value (negate and subtract 1)\n4. Position EDI at end of string (before null terminator)\n5. Set direction flag (STD) to scan backward\n6. Use REPNE SCASB to scan backward from end of string looking for matching character\n7. Adjust EDI pointer and compare character at found position\n8. If match found at current position, return pointer; otherwise return NULL\n\nParameters:\npString (char *) - Pointer to null-terminated string to search\nsearchChar (int) - Character value to find (compared as byte)\n\nReturns:\nPointer to last occurrence of searchChar in pString, or NULL if not found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns NULL if searchChar not found in string\n- Uses standard string length calculation with SCASB instruction\n- Backward scan uses STD flag to search from end toward beginning\n- Character comparison uses raw byte value from searchChar parameter",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:21a12b03112be7c0452f1f2140b0fec9",
