      "name": "HandleScreenshotSaveError",
      "signature": "void HandleScreenshotSaveError(int nErrorCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Handles fatal errors during screenshot save operations by displaying an error dialog and terminating the application.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if file path pointer (ESI) is NULL\n2. If NULL, use error string ID 0x59 (generic error)\n3. If path exists, validate it with Ordinal_10105\n4. If validation succeeds, return without action\n5. If validation fails, copy file path using Ordinal_276 (StringCchCopyA)\n6. Use error string ID 0x5f (file path error)\n7. Load localized error string using Ordinal_10265\n8. Display error message box using Ordinal_10024 with source file info\n9. Terminate application with _exit(-1)\n\nParameters:\n  nErrorCode: Error code from screenshot save operation (passed on stack)\n  pFilePath: File path string pointer (passed implicitly in ESI register)\n\nReturns:\n  void: Function terminates application, only returns if validation succeeds\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL file path triggers generic error 0x59\n  - Valid file path but save failed triggers path error 0x5f\n  - Source file reference: \"..\\Source\\D2Win\\Src\\D2WinMain.c\"\n  - Screenshot format string: \"oScreenshot%03d.jpg\"",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:b26ddfbb9b86d061f617ca3c147982f4",
