      "name": "ClearListNodeCallbacks",
      "signature": "void ClearListNodeCallbacks(int * pListContainer, int depth)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Clears all callback pointers from a linked list node at specified depth.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate that pListContainer is non-null and points to a structure with type ID 4\n2. Verify that depth does not exceed available linked list depth (offset 0x54)\n3. Traverse the linked list from offset 0x48, following 0x1c pointers for depth iterations\n4. Check that traversal reached the target node and counter matches requested depth\n5. Iterate through 5 callback slots (offsets 0, 4, 8, 12, 16) in the node\n6. For each non-zero callback, invoke CallIndirectDynamicFunction and clear the pointer\n7. Return after processing all 5 callbacks\n\nParameters:\n  pListContainer (ECX): Pointer to list structure; offset +0x00 must equal 4 (type ID)\n  depth (EDX): Depth in linked list; validated against offset +0x54 max depth\n\nReturns:\n  void; exits with error code -1 if validation fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Calls _exit(-1) if pListContainer is null, type ID != 4, or depth out of bounds\n  - Calls _exit(-1) if linked list traversal cannot reach requested depth\n  - Callbacks cleared after invocation via CallIndirectDynamicFunction",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:c03d3b8d06e6d457dcf3940f583be46e",
