      "name": "TruncateUnicodeStringToPixelWidth",
      "signature": "int TruncateUnicodeStringToPixelWidth(wchar_t * pWideString, int maxPixelWidth)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Truncate a Unicode string to fit within a maximum pixel width\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get the total string length using Unicode::strlen\n2. Return 0 immediately if string is empty or negative length\n3. Iterate through each character position from start to end\n4. For each position, measure the accumulated pixel width of all characters up to that point\n5. Skip newline characters (0x0A) when calculating pixel width\n6. For non-newline characters, call function pointer at DAT_6f901508 to get character metrics\n7. Extract character width from offset +0x3 of the returned structure\n8. Accumulate pixel widths until reaching the specified maxPixelWidth threshold\n9. Return the truncation index where pixel width would be exceeded\n10. Null-terminate the string at the truncation point\n\nParameters:\npWideString - Pointer to wide character string buffer (2 bytes per character)\nmaxPixelWidth - Maximum pixel width constraint for the string\n\nReturns:\nThe character index where the string should be truncated to fit within maxPixelWidth\nReturns 0 if the string is empty or has invalid length\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Newline characters (0x0A) do not contribute to pixel width calculation\n- Function pointer at DAT_6f901508 returns structure with character metrics\n- Character width is stored at offset +0x3 as a single byte\n- String is modified in-place with null termination at truncation point",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:8e5c61c63fb3b55db6e218ddd29f9e9a",
