      "name": "CalculateUnitAnimationFrame",
      "signature": "uint CalculateUnitAnimationFrame(UnitAny * * ppUnit)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Calculate and update animation frame for a unit based on elapsed time and animation parameters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate unit pointer is not null (error 0x4d0 if null)\n2. Verify unit type equals 4 (error 0x4d1 if incorrect type)\n3. Check unit has required animation flags set in gdwBitMasks\n4. Verify unit has frames available (dwTotalFrames > 0)\n5. If animation started flag (0x1) set at offset +0x5c:\n   a. Calculate adjusted time: (dwPosY - dwPosX) + DAT_6f90148c\n   b. Call Ordinal_10184 and SetAnimationDelayByDifficulty for timing adjustments\n   c. Compute frame index: (adjustedTime - dwCurrentFrame) / (animSpeed + dwAnimSpeed) + dwBaseFrame\n   d. Handle loop flag (0x8): clamp frame to valid range [0, dwTotalFrames-1]\n   e. Handle non-loop: set frame to -1 if out of bounds\n   f. Store result in dwCalculatedFrame at offset +0x60\n6. If event handler exists at offset +0x34, invoke it with ppUnit parameter\n7. Return event handler result or 0 if no handler\n\nParameters:\nppUnit - Pointer to pointer to UnitAny structure containing animation state\n\nReturns:\nResult from event handler callback if present, otherwise 0\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Error 0x4d0: Null unit pointer - logs error and calls exit(-1)\n- Error 0x4d1: Invalid unit type (not type 4) - logs error and calls exit(-1)\n- dwCalculatedFrame set to -1 when frame exceeds valid range in non-looping mode\n- Loop flag (0x8) causes frame wrapping within [0, dwTotalFrames-1]\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name          Type     Description\n+0x00   4     dwType              dword    Unit type, must equal 4\n+0x08   4     dwFlags             dword    Unit flags checked against gdwBitMasks\n+0x10   4     dwPosX              dword    X position used in time calculation\n+0x18   4     dwPosY              dword    Y position used in time calculation\n+0x34   4     pEventHandler       pointer  Function pointer to event handler callback\n+0x44   4     dwCurrentFrame      dword    Current animation frame counter\n+0x54   4     dwTotalFrames       dword    Total frames in animation sequence\n+0x58   4     dwBaseFrame         dword    Base frame offset for animation\n+0x5c   4     dwAnimFlags         dword    Animation control flags (bit 0=started, bit 3=loop)\n+0x60   4     dwCalculatedFrame   dword    Calculated output frame index\n+0x94   4     pAnimSeq            pointer  Animation sequence data pointer\n+0xa8   4     dwAnimSpeed         dword    Animation speed modifier",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:53e919e74d6c5d09765bcd6e6b807085",
