      "name": "CloseGameResources",
      "signature": "void CloseGameResources(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Closes all open game resource handles and performs cleanup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Iterate through 8 distinct DLL handle storage locations:\n   - g_pD2DataDllHandle (0x6f9a9ccc)\n   - g_pD2SpeechDllHandle (0x6f9a9cd4)\n   - g_pD2SfxDllHandle (0x6f9a9cb8)\n   - g_pD2DeltaDllHandle (0x6f9a9cbc)\n   - g_pD2KoreanFixupDllHandle (0x6f9a9cd0)\n   - g_pD2ExpansionDllHandle (0x6f9a9ce4)\n   - g_pUnknownDllHandle (0x6f9a9cb4)\n   - g_pPatchD2DllHandle (0x6f9a9ce0)\n2. For each handle pointer location:\n   - Check if handle pointer is non-null\n   - If valid, load the handle value (first DWORD at pointer)\n   - If handle is non-zero, close it via CloseHandle()\n   - Zero the handle value at pointer location\n   - Invoke callback via CallIndirectDynamicFunction() with parameters:\n     * ECX = handle pointer address\n     * EDX = 0x6f8fd150 (source file path string)\n     * Stack params: (0, 0x26e)\n   - Nullify the global handle pointer\n3. Call CleanupResourceHandles() for final resource cleanup\n4. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone (void function)\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Handles NULL handle pointers gracefully (skips processing)\n- Handles zero handle values gracefully (skips CloseHandle call)\n- Each handle pointer is validated before dereferencing\n- Callback invocation occurs even if handle was zero (for event logging)\n- CleanupResourceHandles() performs additional cleanup beyond DLL handles\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\n- CloseHandle: Win32 API for closing handles\n- CallIndirectDynamicFunction: Event notification callback dispatcher\n- CleanupResourceHandles: Final cleanup routine for additional resources\n- 8 global DLL handle pointer variables (g_p*DllHandle)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x26e: Event code parameter for callback (likely resource closure event ID)\n- 0x6f8fd150: Source file path string \"../Source/D2Hell/SRC/Archive.cpp\"\n- 8: Total number of DLL handle storage locations processed",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:b31a5633092c931a42640380f02f0563",
