      "name": "BuildLocalizedFilePath",
      "signature": "char * BuildLocalizedFilePath(char * pFilePath, uint resourceId)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Builds a localized file path by concatenating input path with resource string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate offset delta for buffer addressing (local_104 - pFilePath pointer)\n2. Copy input path (pFilePath) to local buffer at adjusted offset\n3. Find end of input path string by scanning for null terminator\n4. Call Ordinal_10070(resourceId) to retrieve resource string pointer\n5. Find end of resource string by scanning for null terminator\n6. Get destination buffer end position by scanning from stack location\n7. Calculate resource string length (pStringEnd - pResourceString)\n8. Copy DWORD blocks: iterate (length >> 2) times copying 4 bytes per iteration\n9. Copy remaining bytes: iterate (length & 3) times copying 1 byte per iteration\n10. Call CreateAndSaveScreenshotFile with null file handle and null parameters\n11. Call Ordinal_10006 with buffer pointer, magic code 0x42, flags 0xffffffff, priority 0\n12. Return hardcoded string pointer to s____Source_D2Win_Src_D2WinArchive\n\nParameters:\npFilePath: Input file path string to concatenate with resource string data\nresourceId: Resource identifier passed to Ordinal_10070 to retrieve resource string data\n\nReturns:\nchar*: Pointer to static string constant s____Source_D2Win_Src_D2WinArchive\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Local buffer localBuffer sized 260 bytes for path + extension storage\n- Concatenation uses pointer arithmetic with offset delta calculation\n- Copies use DWORD-aligned (MOVSD) and byte-aligned (MOVSB) operations for efficiency\n- Magic number 0x42 passed to Ordinal_10006 represents operation code for formatting\n- Flag 0xffffffff (-1) passed to Ordinal_10006 enables all formatting options\n- Return value is always static string pointer, never the constructed local path\n- File handle and buffer parameters to Ordinal_10006 are always null/zero",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:cc4d6dba528ea03c61b5daa66e2cd234",
