      "signature": "void CalculateSkillTier(void * pEntity, int nSkillValue, int nModifier, int nMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Calculates skill tier based on skill value and game mode\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check mode flag (param_4): determines threshold values for tier classification\n2. When mode=0: Use thresholds [4, 8, 12] for tier progression\n3. When mode\u22600: Use thresholds [5, 10, 15] for tier progression\n4. For mode=0: if skillValue < 4 \u2192 tier=0; if < 8 \u2192 tier=1; if < 12 \u2192 tier=2; else tier=3\n5. For mode\u22600: if skillValue < 5 \u2192 tier=0; if < 10 \u2192 tier=1; if < 15 \u2192 tier=2; else tier=3\n6. If modifier flag (param_3) is set and tier > 0, add 3 to tier (tier += 3)\n7. Call Ordinal_10132 to apply calculated tier to entity\nParameters:\n  pEntity [ESP+0x4]: Entity/object pointer to apply skill tier to\n  nSkillValue [ESP+0x8]: Raw skill value used for tier calculation\n  nModifier [ESP+0xC]: Modifier flag; if set, adds 3 to non-zero tiers\n  nMode [ESP+0x10]: Mode flag; 0=standard thresholds, non-zero=alternate thresholds\nReturns:\n  void - applies tier value to entity via Ordinal_10132 call\nSpecial Cases:\n  Tier 0 is returned for low skill values (below first threshold)\n  Tier values range from 0-3 in standard path, 3-6 when modifier is applied\n  Modifier adds 3 only when both conditions met: modifier\u22600 AND tier>0",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
