      "name": "GetOrCreateScreenshotCacheNode",
      "signature": "ScreenshotCacheNode * GetOrCreateScreenshotCacheNode(DWORD dwParam2, LPVOID lpOutputBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Get or create a screenshot cache node with reference counting\n\nThis function implements a screenshot cache using a doubly-linked list.\nIt searches for an existing cache node matching three parameters, or\ncreates a new node if not found. Each node stores a screenshot file\nhandle and image data pointer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Search linked list at DAT_6f9a9e34 for matching node (compare dwParam1, dwParam2, dwParam3)\n2. If found, increment reference count and return existing node\n3. If not found, allocate 0x42c bytes for new ScreenshotCacheNode\n4. Initialize all node fields to zero\n5. Set node parameters (dwParam1 from EBX, dwParam2 from stack, dwParam3 from EDI)\n6. Increment reference count to 1\n7. Call CreateAndSaveScreenshotFile(0, &pFileHandle) to create screenshot\n8. Validate image format byte at offset +3 equals 0x14\n9. Store image data handle in node at offset +0x14\n10. Link new node at head of doubly-linked list\n11. Update global list head pointer DAT_6f9a9e34\n12. Return pointer to cache node\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT EBX = dwParam1 - First parameter for cache key matching\n  dwParam2 - Second parameter for cache key matching (passed on stack)\n  IMPLICIT EDI = dwParam3 - Third parameter for cache key matching\n  lpOutputBuffer - Output buffer pointer passed to CreateAndSaveScreenshotFile\n\nReturns:\n  Pointer to ScreenshotCacheNode (either existing or newly created)\n  Exits process on failure (CreateAndSaveScreenshotFile fails or format invalid)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Error 0x3e1: CreateAndSaveScreenshotFile returned NULL\n  - Error 0x3ea: Image format byte at offset +3 is not 0x14\n  - Both errors trigger Ordinal_10024 logging and _exit(-1)\n  - Reference count starts at 1 for new nodes, increments for existing\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset | Size | Field Name     | Type    | Description\n  -------|------|----------------|---------|----------------------------------\n  0x00   | 4    | refCount       | int     | Reference counter (incremented on reuse)\n  0x04   | 4    | dwParam1       | DWORD   | First cache key parameter (from EBX)\n  0x08   | 4    | dwParam2       | DWORD   | Second cache key parameter (from stack)\n  0x0C   | 4    | dwParam3       | DWORD   | Third cache key parameter (from EDI)\n  0x10   | 4    | pFileHandle    | pointer | Screenshot file handle\n  0x14   | 4    | pImageData     | pointer | Image data handle/pointer\n  0x18   | 4    | pPrev          | pointer | Previous node in doubly-linked list\n  0x1C   | 4    | pNext          | pointer | Next node in doubly-linked list\n  -------|------|----------------|---------|----------------------------------\n  Total: 32 bytes (0x20)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:c386acfe34529684500b903cc050b314",
