      "name": "LoadPaletteAndInitializeColorTables",
      "signature": "uint LoadPaletteAndInitializeColorTables(char * szPalettePath)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Loads palette file and initializes color lookup tables for rendering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call CreateAndSaveScreenshotFile to get RGB palette data pointer\n2. Build 256-entry RGBA color table with alpha=0 from RGB triplets\n3. Open palette file using Ordinal_10102, exit with error if open fails\n4. Validate file handle is non-zero, exit with error 0x59 if null\n5. Read palette data from file using Ordinal_10105\n6. On read failure, copy local buffer and exit with error 0x5f\n7. Allocate 0xcf-sized buffer using Ordinal_10042 for palette data\n8. Call ValidateScreenshotParameters to verify palette buffer integrity\n9. Exit with error 0x49 if validation fails\n10. Close file handle using Ordinal_10103\n11. Copy palette buffer to 11 global arrays at different offsets:\n    - DAT_6f922338 (0x400 bytes, offset +0x0)\n    - DAT_6f93db60 (0x30000 bytes, offset +0xd40)\n    - DAT_6f932a38 (0x3100 bytes, offset +0x100)\n    - DAT_6f911630 (0x10000 bytes, offset +0x10d40)\n    - DAT_6f901630 (0x10000 bytes, offset +0xcd40)\n    - DAT_6f934a38 (0x1000 bytes, offset +0x900)\n    - DAT_6f935a38 (0x100 bytes, offset +0xd00)\n    - DAT_6f935b60 (0x8000 bytes, offset +0x14d40)\n    - DAT_6f922738 (0x10000 bytes, offset +0x16d40)\n    - DAT_6f932838 (0x100 bytes, offset +0x1ad40)\n    - DAT_6f935b38 (0x27 bytes, offset +0x1ad80)\n    - DAT_6f921638 (0xd00 bytes, offset +0x6b627)\n12. Set alpha channel to 5 for all 256 palette entries\n13. Generate two color index tables by scaling RGB values:\n    - Scale to 170% brightness (0xaa/100) clamped to 0xff\n    - Store in DAT_6f932738 using Ordinal_10049\n    - Create red-only table in DAT_6f932938 (R channel, GB=0)\n14. Call InitializePointerArraysAndCallOrdinal10022 to set up data structures\n15. Call Ordinal_10061 with base palette pointer\n16. Call Ordinal_10043 twice with codes 0x96 and 0x99\n17. Return 1 for success\n\nParameters:\n- palettePath: Path to palette data file (.dat or .pl2 format)\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on success\n- Exits process with -1 on file errors\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Error 0x59: File open failure\n- Error 0x5f: File read failure\n- Error 0x49: Palette validation failure\n- RGB values scaled by 170/255 for brightness adjustment\n- All RGB components clamped to 0xff maximum",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
