      "name": "InitializePaletteAndColorTables",
      "signature": "uint InitializePaletteAndColorTables(int nPaletteMode, char * pszPalettePath)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes game color palettes and color lookup tables.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if nPaletteMode is 0 (use default Act 1 palette)\n2. If mode 0: Format default palette file paths using sprintf\n   - Build path for palette ACT file (palette_act1.pal.dat)\n   - Build path for palette PL2 file (palette_act1.pal.pl2)\n3. Load the palette file using LoadPaletteAndInitializeColorTables\n4. Initialize all color lookup tables using InitializeColorTables\n5. Return 1 on success\n\nParameters:\n- nPaletteMode: Palette selection mode (0=default Act 1, non-zero=custom)\n- pszPalettePath: Path to custom palette file when nPaletteMode != 0\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Always returns success (palette initialization completed)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Mode 0 uses hardcoded Act 1 palette files from DATA_GLOBAL directory\n- Custom palette path ignored when nPaletteMode is 0\n- Both InitializeColorTables calls occur regardless of mode selection\n\nStructure Layout:\n- Local stack buffers: 260 bytes each for palette file paths\n- Total local stack space: 520 bytes (0x208)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:fac73a858a12808be110554ec05ee2a1",
