      "name": "InitializePaletteAndGraphics",
      "signature": "uint InitializePaletteAndGraphics(uint paletteIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Initializes palette and graphics subsystem for the specified palette index.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract palette index from lower 8 bits of input parameter and add 1\n2. Validate palette index range [1-5]; clamp to 1 if out of bounds\n3. Format primary palette file path using index (DATA/GLOBAL.xx, palette index, pal_dat)\n4. Format secondary palette file path using index (DATA/GLOBAL.xx, palette index, pal_pl2)\n5. Load palette from secondary path and initialize color tables\n6. Copy graphics buffer to target and invoke graphics vtable at offset 0x70\n7. Return palette initialization result\n\nParameters:\npaletteIndex: Input palette index (0-255 range, lower 8 bits extracted)\n\nReturns:\nuint: Result of palette initialization (0=success, non-zero=error code)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Palette index automatically clamped to range [1-5]\n- Out-of-range indices default to palette 1\n- Function constructs file paths dynamically using sprintf\n- Palette files: pal_dat (primary data), pal_pl2 (secondary data)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:2cec2651d65d8936907a543ea870477c",
