      "name": "BlitScaledRectangle",
      "signature": "void BlitScaledRectangle(tagRECT * pSourceRect, tagRECT * pDestRect, uint blitParam)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Blits a source rectangle to a destination rectangle with optional scaling\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load source and destination rectangle dimensions from RECT structures\n2. Calculate source width (srcWidth = right - left) and height (srcHeight = bottom - top)\n3. Calculate destination width and height from pDestRect (passed implicitly in EAX)\n4. Check if dimensions match exactly (srcWidth == destWidth && srcHeight == destHeight)\n5. If dimensions match, perform direct blit call to Ordinal_10079 with 0x100 offset\n6. If dimensions differ, calculate scale factors: xScaleFactor = (destWidth + srcWidth - 1) / srcWidth, yScaleFactor = (destHeight + srcHeight - 1) / srcHeight\n7. Compute initial Y offset as (pDestRect->top - pSourceRect->top) + 0x100\n8. Execute nested loop: outer loop iterates yScaleFactor times, inner loop iterates xScaleFactor times\n9. For each iteration, calculate clipped boundaries ensuring output stays within destination bounds\n10. Call Ordinal_10079 with computed offsets and clipped rectangle parameters\n11. Increment X offset by srcWidth for each inner iteration, Y offset by srcHeight for outer iteration\n\nParameters:\n  pSourceRect - Pointer to source rectangle structure\n    +0x0: left (LONG) - Source left X coordinate\n    +0x4: top (LONG) - Source top Y coordinate  \n    +0x8: right (LONG) - Source right X coordinate\n    +0xc: bottom (LONG) - Source bottom Y coordinate\n  pDestRect - Pointer to destination rectangle (passed in EAX, implicit parameter)\n    +0x0: left (LONG) - Destination left X coordinate\n    +0x4: top (LONG) - Destination top Y coordinate\n    +0x8: right (LONG) - Destination right X coordinate\n    +0xc: bottom (LONG) - Destination bottom Y coordinate\n  blitParam - Parameter passed through to Ordinal_10079 blit function\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value, performs side effects via Ordinal_10079\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Magic number 0x100 (256): Offset added to Y coordinate for blit positioning\n  - Direct blit path: When source and destination dimensions are identical\n  - Scaling path: When dimensions differ, uses tiled blitting approach\n  - Clipping: Output coordinates clamped to destination rectangle boundaries\n  - Scale calculation: Uses ceiling division ((dest + src - 1) / src) for tile count\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n-------|------|------------|------|------------------------------------------\n   0x0 |    4 | left       | LONG | Left boundary X coordinate\n   0x4 |    4 | top        | LONG | Top boundary Y coordinate\n   0x8 |    4 | right      | LONG | Right boundary X coordinate\n   0xc |    4 | bottom     | LONG | Bottom boundary Y coordinate\nTotal size: 16 bytes (0x10)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:0e2bf0e2cd2034bcb7dbc2142d9f5272",
