      "name": "RemoveUIControlFromCache",
      "signature": "int RemoveUIControlFromCache(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Removes a cached UI control from the UI control list and clears the global reference.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the cached UI control pointer from global variable gpCachedUIControl\n2. Initialize return status to 0 (no removal performed)\n3. If cached control pointer is not null:\n   a. Call RemoveUIControlFromList to remove the control from the linked list\n   b. Clear the global variable to null\n   c. Propagate the removal status from RemoveUIControlFromList\n4. Return removal status (0 if no control was cached, 1 if successfully removed)\n\nReturns:\nint - Status code: 0 if no cached control existed, 1 if control was successfully removed and cleared from the list\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If gpCachedUIControl is already null, function returns 0 without calling RemoveUIControlFromList\n- RemoveUIControlFromList may also update other global UI control references if they point to the same control\n- The global reference is always cleared to null, ensuring no stale pointers remain\n\nStructure Layout - UI Control (accessed via RemoveUIControlFromList):\nOffset  Size  Field Name              Type      Description\n+0x00   4     (fields 0-14)          int*      Control linked list structure (specific fields not analyzed)\n+0x3C   4     pNextControl           int*      Pointer to next control in linked list (offset +0x0F = +0x3C/4)\n\nGlobal Variables:\ngpCachedUIControl @ 0x6f9a9e24 - Cached pointer to UI control pending removal",
