      "name": "CreateDropdownMenuControl",
      "signature": "void CreateDropdownMenuControl(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Creates and initializes a dropdown menu (listbox) UI control and links it into the game object list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if a dropdown menu control already exists at DAT_6f9a9e24\n   - If exists, call RemoveUIControlFromList to clean it up and clear the pointer\n2. Allocate 0x464 bytes (0x29 dwords) of memory via AllocateMemory(0x29, 0)\n3. Store allocation result in DAT_6f9a9e24 for global reference\n4. Zero-initialize the allocated memory with REP STOSD (0x11a iterations = 282 dwords)\n5. Initialize structure fields:\n   - [EDX+0x0] = 0xb (control type identifier for dropdown menu)\n   - [EDX+0x8] = Combined bit masks from gdwBitMasks_exref offsets 0x0, 0x8, 0xc\n   - [EDX+0xc] = DAT_6f901488 (render data pointer)\n   - [EDX+0x10] = DAT_6f90148c (click data pointer)\n   - [EDX+0x1c] = RenderDropdownMenuControl function pointer\n   - [EDX+0x20] = ProcessListBoxClick function pointer\n   - [EDX+0x24] through [EDX+0x34] = 0 (clear control state fields)\n   - [EDX+0x3c] = 0 (next pointer, will be set when linking)\n   - [EDX+0x464] = 0xffffffff (sentinel value at end of structure)\n6. Link the new control into the game object list:\n   - If gpGameObjectListHead is NULL, set it to the new control\n   - Otherwise, traverse the linked list to find the last node and append the new control\n\nReturns:\nNone (void function). Modifies global pointers: DAT_6f9a9e24 (dropdown control), gpGameObjectListHead (object list).\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If a dropdown already exists, it is properly cleaned up via RemoveUIControlFromList before allocation\n- Uses 0x464 (1124 decimal) as structure size, allocated as 0x29 (41) dwords with REP STOSD initialization\n- Sentinel value 0xffffffff at offset 0x464 may mark structure boundary\n- Control is linked at offset 0x3c which appears to be a next pointer for doubly-linked or single-linked list traversal",
