      "name": "WriteScreenshotToFile",
      "signature": "int WriteScreenshotToFile(UnitAny * pScreenshotObj, char * pFilePath)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "WriteScreenshotToFile - Write screenshot game object data to a file\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pScreenshotObj pointer is not NULL\n2. Initialize local variables: nBufferSize=0x100, pBuffer, pFileHandle\n3. Calculate screenshot data buffer at pScreenshotObj+0x40 (size 0x100 bytes)\n4. Open or create file at pFilePath with 0x100 byte buffer\n5. Write screenshot buffer (0x100 bytes) to file\n6. Write additional data at pScreenshotObj+0x140 (0x104 bytes) to file\n7. Close file handle and return 1 on success\n8. Return 0 on failure or write errors\n\nParameters:\npScreenshotObj - Pointer to screenshot game object with structure:\n                 +0x0: Type field (validated elsewhere as type 9)\n                 +0x40: Screenshot bitmap buffer (256 bytes)\n                 +0x140: Additional screenshot metadata (260 bytes)\npFilePath - Null-terminated path string for output file\n\nReturns:\n1 on successful file write\n0 on failure (file open/write error)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nNone documented - assumes valid pScreenshotObj and writable pFilePath\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name          Type    Description\n0x0     4     dwType              uint    Object type identifier\n0x40    256   screenshotBuffer    char[]  Main screenshot bitmap data\n0x140   260   screenshotMetadata  char[]  Additional metadata/palette",
