      "name": "CreateGameObject",
      "signature": "undefined4 * CreateGameObject(int screenWidth, int screenHeight, int sizeHeight, int sizeWidth, undefined4 objectType)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a new game object node (screenshot/display object).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x150 bytes (336 bytes) via Ordinal_10042 memory allocator\n2. Zero-initialize entire allocated buffer using REP STOSD (84 dwords)\n3. Extract base flags from offset +0x8 and store in flags variable\n4. Set object type field (offset +0x0) to 9\n5. Load flag masks from gdwBitMasks global (offsets +0x0 and +0x8)\n6. Apply flag masks to object flags field\n7. Initialize core object fields: position, size, and callback handlers\n8. Calculate center coordinates from screen dimensions and offsets\n9. Link object into global game object list using next pointer at offset +0x3c\n10. Return pointer to newly created object\n\nParameters:\n  screenWidth - Screen/window width in pixels (stored at offset +0xc)\n  screenHeight - Screen/window height in pixels (stored at offset +0x10)\n  sizeHeight - Object height in pixels (stored at offset +0x14)\n  sizeWidth - Object width in pixels (stored at offset +0x18)\n  objectType - Object type/behavior identifier (stored at offset +0x34)\n\nReturns:\n  Pointer to newly allocated and initialized game object (336 bytes)\n  NULL only if memory allocation fails (rare)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Magic offsets: 0x1d4 (468 decimal - screen offset) and 0x3c (60 decimal - next ptr)\n  Global list: gpGameObjectListHead maintains linked list of all game objects\n  List traversal: Walks list using offset +0x3c until finding NULL next pointer\n  Screenshot callbacks: ProcessScreenshotObject (offset +0x1c) and InvokeScreenshotCallback (offset +0x24)\n\nStructure Layout (Game Object):\nOffset  Size  Field Name              Type       Description\n0x00    4     objectType              uint       Object type flag (set to 9)\n0x04    4     flags                   uint       Combined capability flags\n0x08    4     flagMask                uint       Flags from gdwBitMasks\n0x0c    4     screenWidth             int        Screen width coordinate\n0x10    4     screenHeight            int        Screen height coordinate\n0x14    4     sizeHeight              int        Object height in pixels\n0x18    4     sizeWidth               int        Object width in pixels\n0x1c    4     processCallback         fn_ptr     ProcessScreenshotObject function\n0x24    4     invokeCallback          fn_ptr     InvokeScreenshotCallback function\n0x34    4     objectTypeInfo          uint       Additional type information\n0x3c    4     nextObject              ptr        Next object in linked list\n0x140   16    centerCoords            int[4]     Calculated center X/Y coordinates\nTotal: 336 bytes allocated (0x150)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
