      "name": "RenderFramedText",
      "signature": "void RenderFramedText(void * this, void * pThis, int yPosition, int alignmentMode, int textColor)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Renders text within multiple frames with automatic spacing calculation and alignment.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetFrameCount() on the object to determine number of frames to render\n2. Clear the frame buffer (52 bytes) using REP STOSD to initialize array\n3. Determine alignment mode: if alignmentMode == 1 (center), calculate centered spacing; if alignmentMode == 2 (right), calculate right-aligned spacing\n4. If alignment mode is 1 or 2: iterate through each frame, call GetRenderingDeviceContext() and GetRegionBounds() to get frame dimensions, accumulate total spacing in totalSpacing\n5. Apply spacing calculation: mode 1 (center) = -1 - (totalSpacing >> 1); mode 2 (right) = -totalSpacing\n6. Adjust yPosition by adding calculated spacing offset\n7. Iterate through all frames again with frameIndex from 0 to frameCount-1\n8. For each frame: set frameBuffer[0] = frameIndex, then call either RenderUIText() if colorMode == -1, or Ordinal_10019() for custom color rendering\n9. Increment frameIndex and advance yPosition by 0x100 (256 pixels) for next frame\n10. Return void\n\nParameters:\n- pThis: Pointer to rendering context object (passed in ECX, implicit this pointer)\n- yPosition: Starting Y-coordinate for text rendering\n- alignmentMode: Text alignment: 1=center, 2=right, other=no alignment adjustment\n- textColor: Color value to use for text rendering\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic offset 0x100 (256 pixels) is the vertical spacing between frames\n- Frame buffer array is 52 bytes (13 DWORDs)\n- colorMode value of -1 triggers default color rendering path\n- Center alignment uses right-shift by 1 (division by 2) for centered offset calculation",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:9aea14a4baa1be41e84841f701d5518a",
