      "signature": "void MarshalParameterValue(undefined4 dataValue, undefined4 configValue, undefined4 resultAddress)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Imported ordinal stub that marshals parameter values to an external helper function.\n\nThis is a thin wrapper (JMP instruction) that delegates to an external DLL function. \nThe function is called by parameter marshaling code to process and validate data values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Jump to external helper function implementation\n2. External function processes dataValue, configValue, and resultAddress\n3. Returns control to caller\n\nParameters:\n- dataValue: Primary data value to be marshaled/processed\n- configValue: Configuration or context parameter for marshaling operation\n- resultAddress: Address or identifier for where result should be stored\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No direct return value; external function performs operation via side effects\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- This is an ordinal import stub (JMP dword ptr [0x6f8fb0d0])\n- External implementation in imported DLL\n- Called from parameter marshaling infrastructure",
