      "name": "CalculateUITextWidth",
      "signature": "uint CalculateUITextWidth(Unicode * pText, int xPosition, uint yPosition, int charWidth, uint fontIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Calculates and renders Unicode text with formatting codes to UI position.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Validate font index parameter (fontIndex >= 0)\\n2. Call Ordinal_10078 to get current font type\\n3. Calculate string length using Unicode::strlen\\n4. Initialize 52-byte render buffer with zeros\\n5. Iterate through each Unicode character in string:\\n   a. Load 2-byte Unicode character from string\\n   b. Check if character value < 0x100 (ASCII range)\\n   c. If character == 0xFF, check for format codes ('\\\\0' or '\\\\c')\\n   d. If format code found, process special rendering instruction\\n   e. Otherwise, render character at current position with width calculation\\n6. Handle newline character (0x0A) by moving Y position to next line\\n7. For regular characters, call GetRenderingDeviceContext and Ordinal_10000\\n8. Render character using Ordinal_10074 with position bounds checking\\n9. Accumulate character width and advance X position\\n\\nParameters:\\npText - Pointer to Unicode string (16-bit characters per element)\\nxPosition - Starting X coordinate for text rendering\\nyPosition - Starting Y coordinate for text rendering\\ncharWidth - Maximum character width for bounds checking\\nfontIndex - Font index for character metrics lookup\\n\\nReturns:\\nuint - Total width of rendered text in pixels\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- fontIndex < 0: Returns yPosition unchanged without processing\\n- Format codes: 0xFF0x00 renders as space, 0xFF0x63 ('\\\\c') renders with special formatting\\n- Newline (0x0A): Moves to next line and adjusts Y position based on font height\\n- Text exceeding bounds: Calls Ordinal_10074 with different parameters to handle overflow\\n- Font type 6: Skips GetRenderingDeviceContext call for special font handling",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:5fcd8fccf4dcfdc69f732c072533d061",
