      "name": "InitializeRenderingResources",
      "signature": "void InitializeRenderingResources(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "InitializeRenderingResources - Initialize rendering resource tables\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize pointer to first resource handle table at DAT_6f901514\n2. Loop through handle array (stride 0x14 = 5 DWORDs per entry):\n   a. Load first handle at offset -4 from current position\n   b. If handle is non-zero, call ReleaseResourceHandle to release it\n   c. If handle still non-zero after release, call CallIndirectDynamicFunction\n   d. Zero out the released handle\n   e. Load second handle at current position [ESI]\n   f. If handle is non-zero, call CallIndirectDynamicFunction\n   g. Zero out the second handle\n   h. Move to next entry (add 0x14 to pointer)\n3. After loop completes (all 2 pairs processed), handle final resource at DAT_6f901628:\n   a. Call ReleaseResourceHandle on final resource\n   b. If final resource was non-zero, call CallIndirectDynamicFunction\n   c. Zero out final resource\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Resource table has 2 pairs of handles per entry, organized as:\n  Offset -4: First handle (released first)\n  Offset 0: Second handle (released second)\n- Loop count determined by comparing address to 0x6f90162c boundary\n- Final resource at DAT_6f901628 handled separately after main loop\n- CallIndirectDynamicFunction called conditionally after ReleaseResourceHandle if handle was non-zero\n\nStructure Layout:\nResource Handle Entry Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n-0x4   | 4    | handle1    | uint | First resource handle\n0x0    | 4    | handle2    | uint | Second resource handle\n0x4    | 4    | handle3    | uint | Third resource handle\n0x8    | 4    | handle4    | uint | Fourth resource handle\n0xC    | 4    | handle5    | uint | Fifth resource handle\nTotal: 0x14 bytes (5 DWORDs)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:84d091649fafd9b3c4ed9e80e74412a0",
