      "name": "RenderFormattedUnicodeText",
      "signature": "void RenderFormattedUnicodeText(Unicode * pTextString, int nXPosition, int nYPosition, int nMaxWidth, int nColorIndex, undefined4 renderFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Render Unicode text string with embedded color codes and formatting\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate string length using Unicode::strlen\n2. Adjust initial X position if nMaxWidth parameter is non-zero by calling FUN_6f8f1f00\n3. Initialize glyph rendering buffer (52 bytes on stack) via func_0x7b663370\n4. Loop through each character in the string (index 0 to stringLength-1)\n5. Check if character is special marker (0xff and value < 0x100)\n6. If marker found, read next character and compare with 0x6f9aa670 using Unicode::strncmp\n7. If comparison succeeds, parse color digit (character - 0x30), validate range 0-12, skip 3 chars\n8. If comparison fails, render special glyph via Ordinal_10019 at offset +0x8, advance X by byte at offset +0x3\n9. If character is newline (0xa), reset X position and adjust Y by font height * -16 / 10\n10. For normal characters, call glyph rendering function via DAT_6f901508, render via Ordinal_10019, advance X position\n11. Continue loop until all characters processed\n12. Return to caller (stdcall cleanup of 24 bytes)\n\nParameters:\n  pTextString - Pointer to Unicode string to render with embedded formatting codes\n  nXPosition - Initial X coordinate for text rendering in screen space\n  nYPosition - Initial Y coordinate for text rendering in screen space  \n  nMaxWidth - Maximum width constraint for text (0 = no constraint, non-zero triggers right-align adjustment)\n  nColorIndex - Current text color index (0-12 range, used for rendering glyphs)\n  renderFlags - Rendering flags passed to Ordinal_10019 (blend mode, transparency, etc)\n\nIMPLICIT:\n  EAX - Contains calculated X position after width adjustment\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Color code format: 0xff followed by character compared to 0x6f9aa670, then digit 0-9 (maps to color 0-12)\n  - Invalid color digits (>= 13) reset color to 0\n  - Newline character (0xa) resets X position and advances Y by negative font height offset\n  - Special glyphs rendered when 0xff marker doesn't match color code pattern\n  - Glyph data structure accessed: offset +0x3 = width byte, offset +0x8 = glyph ID word\n  - Font metrics from global: DAT_6f8ffd34 indexes into table at 0x6f901518 (stride 0x14)\n  - Font height byte at offset +0xa in font metrics structure",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:de8222f6079c8303b6f638ab296cd84d",
