      "comment": "Thunk function that adapts calling convention for Ordinal_10055\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Transfer ESI parameter to ECX register\n2. Transfer EAX parameter to EDX register\n3. Restore ESI from stack\n4. Jump to Ordinal_10055 at 0x6f8f2080\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT: ESI - First parameter (transferred to ECX)\nIMPLICIT: EAX - Second parameter (transferred to EDX)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - This is a tail-call thunk that jumps to target function\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- This is a register adapter thunk that converts between calling conventions\n- The actual function logic resides in Ordinal_10055\n- ESI is preserved/restored via stack (POP ESI at 0x6f8f2b2d)\n- Uses tail-call optimization (JMP instead of CALL/RET)",
