      "name": "RenderSelectedTextWithHighlight",
      "signature": "void RenderSelectedTextWithHighlight(Unicode * pSelectedText, int nXPosition, int nYPosition)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Renders selected text with highlighting background color.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call CalculateTextPixelWidth to get width of selected text in pixels\n2. Load color byte from game state array at DAT_6f901518 (offset +0xa)\n3. Call CallGraphicsVtable_0x50WithErrorCheck to initialize graphics context\n4. Check if text width (yPos) + X position exceeds available width (unaff_ESI)\n   - If exceeds, clamp width to available space (unaff_ESI - yPos)\n5. Check if Y position + 0x1f (31) exceeds maximum drawable height (unaff_EBX)\n   - If exceeds, clamp Y position to (unaff_EBX - 0x1f)\n6. Calculate clipping height: iVar1 = param_3 + 2 (add padding)\n7. Check if clipping height minus draw area width is negative\n   - If negative, double the clipping height for buffer allocation\n8. Call HandleInputEvent with calculated bounds and parameters\n9. Call RenderTextWithColorCodes to draw selected text on highlight background\n10. Return void\n\nParameters:\n  pSelectedText - Pointer to Unicode string containing selected text\n  nXPosition - X coordinate for text rendering\n  nYPosition - Y coordinate for text rendering\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Width clamping: Prevents text from extending beyond right edge of control\n  - Height clamping: Prevents text from extending beyond bottom edge of control\n  - Negative height handling: Applies 2x scaling to clipping height when negative\n  - Color source: Loads highlight color from global game state color array",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:c7ca12ba51ad31b776b555e6e931e3f7",
