      "name": "InitializeTextRenderingContext",
      "signature": "void InitializeTextRenderingContext(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Initialize or finalize text rendering context for UI text display.\n\nThis function is a thunk that jumps to an external implementation (likely in a graphics DLL) to prepare or finalize the rendering state for text operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Jump to external text rendering setup function at 0x7b662dd0\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- This function is a simple JMP thunk to an external implementation\n- Called by: RenderTextBoxControl, RenderChatMessageUI, RenderTextInputControl, and other UI text rendering functions\n- Typically called before and after rendering text to synchronize rendering context\n- The actual implementation is in an external DLL (address 0x7b662dd0)\n- Used 35+ times throughout the codebase for text rendering synchronization",
