      "name": "ReadTextFromClipboard",
      "signature": "char * ReadTextFromClipboard(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Read text from Windows clipboard and copy to internal buffer\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if CF_TEXT (format 1) is available on clipboard\n2. If not available, return pointer to empty string\n3. Get window handle from Ordinal_10048 (GetGameWindowHandle)\n4. Open clipboard with window handle\n5. If open fails, return pointer to empty string\n6. Get clipboard data handle for CF_TEXT format\n7. If no data, skip to cleanup\n8. Lock global memory to get pointer to clipboard text\n9. If lock fails, skip to cleanup\n10. Copy up to 0x200 (512) bytes from clipboard to buffer at 0x6f9aa680\n11. Unlock global memory handle\n12. Close clipboard\n13. Return pointer to buffer containing clipboard text\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  char * - Pointer to buffer at 0x6f9aa680 containing clipboard text (512 bytes)\n           Returns pointer to empty string at 0x6f8fc4b7 if clipboard unavailable\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - CF_TEXT format constant: 1 (standard text format)\n  - Buffer size: 0x200 (512 bytes) maximum copy length\n  - Empty string fallback: Points to \"..\\Source\\D2Win\\Src\\D2WinMain.c\" debug string\n  - Buffer address: 0x6f9aa680 (global clipboard text buffer)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
