      "name": "UnloadPentspinCursor",
      "signature": "void UnloadPentspinCursor(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Unloads the pentaspin cursor resource and clears the global handle.\n\nThis function releases the pentaspin cursor that was previously loaded by\nLoadPentspinCursor. It calls the resource release function and performs cleanup\nif the cursor was loaded, then clears the global cursor handle.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save cursor handle from global DAT_6f9014ec to local variable\n2. Call Ordinal_10065 to release the cursor resource (pass handle in ESI)\n3. Check if cursor handle was valid (non-zero)\n4. If valid, call Ordinal_10043 with parameters 0x5c and 0 to perform additional cleanup\n5. Clear global cursor handle DAT_6f9014ec to 0\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Ordinal_10065 is called regardless of whether handle is null (safe to call)\n- Ordinal_10043 only called if cursor was actually loaded (handle != 0)\n- Parameter 0x5c (92 decimal) may indicate cursor resource type identifier\n- Second parameter 0 may indicate standard cleanup mode",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:458c37e05ea78f5bd1096c99df2b7972",
