      "name": "InitializeRenderingParameters",
      "signature": "void InitializeRenderingParameters(tagRECT * pRect)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initialize rendering viewport parameters from rectangle coordinates\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract right coordinate from pRect+0xc as 16-bit word\n2. Extract bottom coordinate from pRect+0xe as 16-bit word\n3. Call Ordinal_10029(1) to enable rendering mode\n4. Call Ordinal_10080 with stack buffers to get adjusted coordinates\n5. Call Ordinal_10051 with register and decremented values\n6. Store bottom coordinate to global DAT_6f90148c\n7. Store right coordinate to global DAT_6f901488\n8. Conditionally call SetCursorPos if coordinates were adjusted\n\nParameters:\n  pRect (tagRECT *) - Pointer to RECT structure containing viewport bounds\n                      Only right (+0xc) and bottom (+0xe) fields are used\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Reads 16-bit words from 32-bit LONG fields (uses lower word only)\n  - Ordinal_10080 may adjust coordinates based on display settings\n  - SetCursorPos only called if coordinate adjustment occurred\n  - Global DAT_6f901488 stores viewport width (right coordinate)\n  - Global DAT_6f90148c stores viewport height (bottom coordinate)\n  - Unreachable code block at 0x6f8f7861 removed by optimizer\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name  Type    Description\n------  ----  ----------  ------  ---------------------------\n+0x0    4     left        LONG    Left edge X coordinate\n+0x4    4     top         LONG    Top edge Y coordinate\n+0x8    4     right       LONG    Right edge X coordinate (used)\n+0xc    4     bottom      LONG    Bottom edge Y coordinate (used)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:e2568697c6e40afa650be4afb7816171",
