      "name": "AddUIControlToFreeList",
      "signature": "uint AddUIControlToFreeList(void * pControl)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Add UI control node to the tail of the free list.\n\nThis function maintains a singly-linked list of freed UI control structures\nthat can be reused. The free list is anchored at DAT_6f9014a4 and nodes are\nlinked via a \"next\" pointer at offset +0x3c.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear the next pointer of the incoming control node (offset +0x3c)\n2. Check if the free list is empty (DAT_6f9014a4 == NULL)\n3. If empty, initialize the list by setting DAT_6f9014a4 to the new control\n4. If not empty, traverse the linked list to find the tail node\n5. Append the new control to the tail by updating the last node's next pointer\n6. Return 1 to indicate success\n\nParameters:\n  pControl (ECX) - Pointer to UI control structure to add to free list\n\nReturns:\n  Always returns 1 (success)\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset | Size | Field      | Type     | Description\n  -------|------|------------|----------|---------------------------\n    +0x3c|    4 | pNext      | void *   | Next node in free list\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - DAT_6f9014a4 is the global free list head pointer\n  - Offset 0x3c is the next pointer field in the UI control structure\n  - The function always succeeds and returns 1",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:3a308c4839616646680ef4678b99be78",
