      "name": "InitializeGame",
      "signature": "int InitializeGame(int nWindow)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes the game engine and sets up core game systems.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if already initialized via flag at 0x6f90149c\n2. If not initialized, check second flag at 0x6f9014d4\n3. If both flags are clear, call Ordinal_10048 (subsystem initialization)\n4. Call Ordinal_10080 to set up initialization data\n5. Call indirect function via 0x6f8fb338 with subsystem parameters\n6. Store hWindow parameter in global flag at 0x6f90149c\n7. Call Ordinal_10104 with parameter 1 (initialization marker)\n8. Call Ordinal_10060 with hWindow and 0 to initialize main subsystem\n9. Test return value; if failed, call Ordinal_10029 (cleanup handler) and exit with code -1\n10. Call Ordinal_10061 to initialize sprite/rendering system\n11. Call Ordinal_10068 to allocate game memory (0x800000 bytes, offset 0x7d000)\n12. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  hWindow (int): Window handle passed to game initialization subsystems\n\nReturns:\n  int: 1 on success, -1 on initialization failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If already initialized (flag 0x6f90149c != 0), skips to hWindow storage step\n  - Initialization failure in Ordinal_10060 triggers cleanup and returns -1\n  - Memory allocation size: 0x800000 bytes (8 MB)\n  - Memory base offset: 0x7d000",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
