      "name": "InitializeSystemParameters",
      "signature": "void InitializeSystemParameters(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initialize system parameters and execute external callback\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if system pointer (DAT_6f9014dc) is initialized\n2. Verify secondary pointer (DAT_6f8ffba0) is valid\n3. Copy coordinate values from DAT_6f901488/6f90148c to DAT_6f9014e0/6f9014e4\n4. Validate and clamp X coordinate (ESI) to ensure >= 0\n5. Validate and clamp Y coordinate (EDX) to ensure >= 0\n6. Push parameters (0, 5, -1, Y-1) onto stack for external call\n7. Execute indirect jump to external handler at 0x02e80000\n8. Initialize 68-byte stack buffer with zeroes using REP STOSD\n9. Set buffer fields with saved system pointer and DAT_6f9014e8\n10. Call Ordinal_10041 with clamped X coordinate and buffer pointer\n11. Clean up stack and return\n\nParameters:\nNone - operates on global state\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If DAT_6f9014dc is NULL, function returns immediately\n- If DAT_6f8ffba0 is NULL, function returns immediately\n- Negative coordinates are clamped to 0\n- Y coordinate is decremented by 1 before external call\n- Magic value 5 pushed as second parameter to external handler\n- Buffer size is 0x48 bytes (72 decimal)\n- Uses indirect jump at 0x02e80000 for external callback\n\nGlobal Data Access:\n- 0x6f9014dc: System pointer (checked, stored in buffer+0x50)\n- 0x6f8ffba0: Secondary validation pointer\n- 0x6f901488: Source X coordinate (ESI)\n- 0x6f90148c: Source Y coordinate (EDX)\n- 0x6f9014e0: Destination X coordinate\n- 0x6f9014e4: Destination Y coordinate\n- 0x6f9014e8: Additional parameter stored in buffer+0x1c",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
