      "name": "InitializeObjectState",
      "signature": "void InitializeObjectState(void * pObject)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes object state by calling Ordinal_10187 and setting initialization flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10187() for system-level initialization\n2. Set state flag at offset +0x18 to 1 (active/initialized)\n3. Set counter/status at offset +0x1c to 0 (reset)\n\nParameters:\n  pObject (void *) - Pointer to object structure being initialized\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Ordinal_10187 may perform global initialization required before object setup\n  - Setting offset +0x18 to 1 marks object as initialized/active\n  - Setting offset +0x1c to 0 resets a counter or status field\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name        | Type  | Description\n-------|------|-------------------|-------|----------------------------------\n +0x18 |    4 | initFlag          | DWORD | Initialization flag (1=initialized)\n +0x1c |    4 | counterOrStatus   | DWORD | Counter or status field (reset to 0)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
