      "name": "DestroyStaticUnicodeObjects",
      "signature": "void DestroyStaticUnicodeObjects(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Destroys static Unicode string objects in memory.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize pointer to static Unicode buffer at 0x6f9aa670\n2. Set iteration count to 2 objects\n3. Loop for each object:\n   a. Call Unicode destructor (dword ptr [0x6f8fb044])\n   b. Advance pointer by 2 bytes to next object\n   c. Decrement counter\n4. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, function performs cleanup only\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Static object count is hardcoded to 2 iterations\n- Each object is 2 bytes in size (likely Unicode character pairs or small objects)\n- Calls virtual destructor via function pointer at 0x6f8fb044\n- This is typically generated by compiler for static initialization/cleanup",
